    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Nike-Partnership-Coordinator_R158579-1": {
      "title": "Nike Partnership Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Nike Partnership Coordinator Department: Business Advancement | Strategic General Administration Job Description The Nike Partnership Coordinator plays a pivotal role in creating and executing brand activation strategies, ensuring seamless implementation of campaigns, events, and initiatives that embody Nike’s values and elevate its brand presence within The Ohio State University community. This individual will collaborate closely with internal teams, external partners, and stakeholders to create dynamic experiences that resonate with university goals and align with Nike’s brand identity. This role will report to the Manager, Affinity, within the Brand Engagement Services & Partnerships unit in Business Advancement. The individual will partner with the Manager, Director, unit and departmental colleagues, and campus-wide stakeholders to lead, coordinate and move strategic programs forward. The highly organized and collaborative teammate will lead the student assistant program, creating an impactful work experience focused on professional development for each cohort. This role will be accountable for delivering measurable brand engagement results, including increasing Nike student program participation, event attendance, and Brand Partnership Impact Study scores. Key job responsibilities: Manage end-to-end planning and delivery of Nike-branded events, activations, and experiential marketing programs, ensuring impactful consumer experiences and brand alignment. Build and maintain strong relationships with key stakeholders to ensure successful collaboration and execution. Provide comprehensive support for Nike and agency partners by managing external tasks critical to partnership and program success, including product ordering, contract-based allotment management, inventory record keeping, and provide additional assistance where needed and requested. Manage campus activations by coordinating communications with campus stakeholders before and after activations, overseeing approval processes, facilitating space reservations and payment, and ensuring seamless execution of all logistical elements for participant safety and experience. Lead and supervise the student assistant program by overseeing hiring, onboarding, professional development, weekly meeting facilitation, timekeeping approval, and the delegation of assignments to ensure efficiency and growth for both the students and program. Contribute to the development of creative concepts for activations, ensuring they reflect Nike’s innovative and forward-thinking brand while maintaining Ohio State brand standards. Identify opportunities for university engagement through Nike activations and the larger Nike partnership. Create annual partnership impact report, in collaboration with Nike and campus stakeholders. The report should recap events to monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of activations, capturing key metrics such as attendance, engagement, and ROI. Minimum Education Requirements Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. Advanced degree in relevant field may be desirable. 4 years of relevant experience required. 4-8 years of relevant experience preferred. Preferred Qualifications Masters degree. Previous experience tracking, monitoring and analyzing qualitative and quantitative data. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills; proven success in sponsorship activation and engagement; experience leading complex, cross-functional projects; and Proven ability to engage and build relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Proficient in MS Office skills and Adobe Creative Suite. FUNCTION: Sales & Customer Service SUBFUNCTION: Event Services CAREER BAND: Specialized CAREER LEVEL: S3 Additional Information: Location: Fawcett Center for Tomorrow (0284) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Rohr-Caf-Manager_R158555-1": {
      "title": "Rohr Café Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Rohr Café Manager Department: Business Advancement | Blackwell Food and Beverage Operations Rohr Café Manager The Blackwell Inn & Pfahl Conference Center – The Ohio State University Are you a hospitality professional who enjoys leading teams, creating exceptional guest experiences, and growing a thriving café operation? Join our team at The Blackwell Inn and take the lead at Rohr Café, a vibrant campus destination located in Mason Hall. If you're energized by customer service, team development, and business growth, this could be the opportunity for you. About the Role As the Rohr Café Manager , you'll oversee the day-to-day operations of Rohr Café while serving as a front-of-house leader and ambassador for exceptional service. Reporting to the Food and Beverage Manager, you'll be responsible for creating a welcoming atmosphere for guests, supporting staff success, and driving operational excellence. This hands-on leadership position offers the opportunity to directly influence the guest experience, grow café revenue through creative promotions and marketing efforts, and help build a high-performing team. You'll work alongside staff, provide coaching and guidance, and ensure the café consistently delivers quality products and service. What You'll Do Lead daily operations of Rohr Café, ensuring efficient service and a positive guest experience Serve as the primary front-of-house leader, working alongside staff to support daily business needs Deliver and promote outstanding customer service through prompt, courteous, and professional interactions Coordinate daily café setup, including transporting supplies and products from off-site locations as needed Drive revenue growth through marketing initiatives, promotional campaigns, and social media engagement Recruit, onboard, train, and develop café team members Provide real-time coaching, performance feedback, and accountability to support service excellence Create staff schedules that align with operational needs and business demands Manage inventory levels and ensure appropriate product availability and stocking Maintain high standards of cleanliness, safety, and sanitation throughout the café Support sustainability initiatives and environmentally responsible operating practices Ensure compliance with university policies and all applicable local and state regulations Maintain and safeguard café equipment and operational resources What Makes You a Great Fit You're passionate about hospitality and creating memorable guest experiences You enjoy leading teams and helping others grow and succeed You're energized by a fast-paced environment where every day is different You have strong organizational skills and can effectively balance multiple priorities You take initiative, solve problems proactively, and focus on continuous improvement You understand how great service, strong operations, and engaged employees contribute to business success Schedule & Flexibility This position requires flexibility to support café operations, including evenings, weekends, and holidays based on business needs. Why Join Us? At The Blackwell Inn, you'll have the opportunity to lead a unique campus café operation while developing your hospitality leadership career at one of the nation's premier public universities. Working at The Blackwell Inn means being part of The Ohio State University community and enjoying: Comprehensive health, dental, and vision benefits Retirement plans with university contributions Generous paid time off and holiday benefits Tuition assistance and educational opportunities Professional development and career growth programs A vibrant campus environment with access to university events, dining, recreation, and Buckeye traditions Join us and help create exceptional experiences for every guest who walks through the doors of Rohr Café. MINIMUM REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. 3 years of relevant experience required. 4-8 years of relevant experience preferred. Additional Information: The target hiring range for this job profile is $ 47,700 - $62,300. The actual salary paid to an individual will vary based on multiple factors, including but not limited to, education, years of experience, internal equity, etc. Function -  Food Service Sub Function -  Hospitality Food and Beverage Services Band -  Managerial Level - M1  Location: Blackwell Inn (0254) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Golf-Course-Superintendent_R158243-1": {
      "title": "Golf Course Superintendent",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Golf Course Superintendent Department: Athletics | Golf Course Administration Job Description The Golf Course Superintendent has primary responsibility to ensure the overall quality and condition of the 36-hole Ohio State University Golf Club. It is to be maintained in a manner to provide the highest level of quality and enjoyment for student-athletes, club members and guests.  This position is responsible for the management and coordination of all maintenance programs and construction projects for the golf course, golf course facilities and grounds; the selection, training and supervision of the golf course operation staff; maintaining golf courses within budgetary guidelines; work with golf club staff in the coordination of events; keep abreast of current innovations in turf management and establish record keeping systems for maintenance scheduling, man-hour accounting, preventive maintenance of equipment, inventory control, pesticide applications, fertilizations, etc. Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. Advanced degree may be desirable. 5 years of relevant experience required. 8-12 years of relevant experience preferred. Possess a working knowledge of golf facility construction principles, practices and methods and a thorough understanding of the rules ands strategies of the game of golf. Minimum of five years experience in the area of golf course management and supervisory responsibility. Pesticide applicator license in category 8 (turf) and category 3 (aquatics).  Desired Qualifications PGA Tour, USGA, OGA, and/or NCAA experience. Experience working with collegiate teams and coaches. Experience collaborating with turfgrass professors with research projects on and off the course. FUNCTION: Facilities, Engineering and Acquisition SUB-FUNCTION: Facilities Operations CAREER BAND: Managerial CAREER LEVEL: M2 Additional Information: Location: OSU Golf Club - Maintenance 1 (0175) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
