    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Health-System-Shared-Services/Senior-Financial-Analyst--CCC-Admin-Offices_R157319-1": {
      "title": "Senior Financial Analyst- CCC Admin Offices",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Senior Financial Analyst- CCC Admin Offices Department: CCC | Administrative Office Job Description Senior Financial Analyst, under the direction of The Ohio State University Comprehensive Cancer Center (OSUCCC) Finance Manager implements day to day administration and analysis of an assigned personal portfolio of approximately 115 OSU funds totaling $16 million each fiscal year within the OSUCCC; performs monthly required financial reconciliations and account analysis and reviews on a wide variety of funds including Endowment, Development, Contract, Earnings (Conference), and General funds; Develops Business Plans for new Faculty recruits and large programs within the Comprehensive Cancer Center; prepares and presents monthly reports and provides financial statements to the OSUCCC Finance Manager, Senior Administrative Staff and Faculty; works cross-functionally with Faculty and Staff in 12 different University Colleges, The James, and all OSU ancillary services to provide support in financial management, budgeting, analytical financial statements, and other financial services; completes monthly reconciliation of payroll transactions on the general ledger and completes HR adjustments and transactions in the University systems as needed; Works directly with Faculty for budgeted HR appointments and management of their staff and students on different University research funds and grants; Processes, reviews, and approves all required financial functions including journals, transfers, deposits, payroll, procurement, and accounts payable; Reviews OSUCCC Contracts, Letters of Offer, and MOUs to appropriately provide financial resources to Faculty and Staff; approves fund availability for financial transactions in compliance with university policies and procedures and the approved delegation of signature authority document; monitors fund balances and alerts Senior Financial Analyst of potential deficits or problems; monitors accounting practices assuring compliance with auditing standards; provides and disseminates information on OSU and CCC departmental fiscal policies and procedures; develops tools and performs account and transaction fluctuation analysis; completes budget to actual data on a monthly, quarterly, and annual bases for fund financial review and forecasting; resolves problems with account details and status; assists with risk assessments and develops risk mitigation plans; performs internal controls assessments and provides recommendations for policies and procedures; works closely with purchasing to resolve any procurement issues with vendors or other departments; utilizes University Human Resources (HR), Financial, and Procurement systems to manage information; maintains fiscal records; Trains Fiscal Associates and assists in providing financial expertise for other staff and areas within the OSUCCC; participates in year-end account closing activities; hires and supervises the student(s) employees as directed by the Finance Manager. Minimum Education Required Bachelor's Level Degree or equivalent combination of education and experience with a Major in accounting or finance Required Qualifications Bachelors Degree in Accounting, Finance, or Business related field and 4 years of financial management experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge of general ledger is required; requires accounting, policy, and finance knowledge, strong analytical skills, computer skills, and the ability to manage time efficiently to complete multiple tasks with competing deadlines; requires successful completion of a background check. Should possess analytical and problem solving skills and demonstrate the ability to work independently and take initiative for process improvement. Needs to demonstrate professionalism, teamwork, and exhibit strong communication skills with all levels of management within the organization, and with internal and external clients. Candidate may be required to complete a pre-employment physical, including a drug screen. Additional Information: Location: Ackerman Rd, 650 (0241) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/James-Cancer-Hospital-and-Solove-Research-Institute/Manager--Registration_R157770-1": {
      "title": "Manager, Registration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Manager, Registration Department: James | Outpatient Registration Scope of Position The Ohio State University Medical Center is committed to improving access and service to customers. The Manager functions as an integral member of the health care team to reflect a culture of cooperation, enthusiasm and mutual respect. The Manager operationalizes the strategic plan of the Medical Center to improve access and services to our customers (consumers and physicians) through centralized scheduling and to ensure reimbursement of hospital services provided. Accurate data is gathered to ensure that proper scheduling is completed for patients being seen at The James. May be responsible for supporting other areas (financial counseling, precertification and registration). Ability to work with multiple different computer systems with different rules and operational methods essential. Must be able to ensure compliance with regulatory requirements. Position Summary The Manager is responsible for managing, guiding, coaching and evaluating the work performance of the staff in Patient Access for The James . Ongoing collaboration with customers that relate directly or indirectly to the department is essential. The Manager assumes primary responsibility for the direct management of staff. The Manager position is responsible for monitoring and ensuring the accuracy of scheduling and efficacy of processes through reports, collecting and coordinating QA data, process analysis and monitoring, developing reporting mechanisms and measuring customer satisfaction. The Manager has an integral role in managing projects related to the product line. The Manager will resolve identified issues and continually move towards improved outcomes. The Manager assists with the development of budgets, implementation of new programs, assures the development of outcome measurements and assures compliance with JCAHO standards and other regulatory agencies. Serves in place of the Assistant Director when unavailable for customers, other departments, and staff. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. Advanced degree may be desirable. 5 years of relevant experience required. 8-12 years of relevant experience preferred. Health care experience preferred. Demonstrated successful leadership, supervisory and management skills. Computer experience required. Knowledge of applications and systems and demonstrates proficiency. Strong demonstrated verbal, written and presentation skills. Sense of professionalism, ability to win confidence of those at various levels of the organization. Career Roadmap FUNCTION: Finance SUB-FUNCTION: Revenue Cycle - Scheduling CAREER BAND: People Leader - Managerial CAREER LEVEL: M2 Additional Information: Location: James Cancer Hospital (0375) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/James-Cancer-Hospital-and-Solove-Research-Institute/Scheduling-Lead-Coordinator_R155748": {
      "title": "Scheduling Lead Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Scheduling Lead Coordinator Department: James | James Ambulatory Clinic Scheduling Scope of Position The Ohio State University Medical Center is committed to improving access and service to customers. The Scheduling Lead Coordinator functions as an integral member of the health care team to reflect a culture of cooperation, enthusiasm and mutual respect. This position ensures access to OSUMC physicians and services and coordinates and supports the functions of integrated access services as well as ensures proper data collection/support for an accurate bill. Additionally, the Patient Access Lead is the product line/service line knowledge expert for product and/or is proficient in scheduling across all scheduling product lines. In addition, the lead is proficient in performing the pre-registration process at the point of scheduling. Position Summary The Scheduling Lead Coordinator is an expert in product or service line area (i.e. physician appt. scheduling, OR/admission, radiology outpatient procedures, full service cardiology scheduling). Responsible for providing consumers (physicians and patients) with accurate, up-to-date information regarding their physicians products, services and general procedures, as well as maintaining software to ensure accuracy of same information. Schedule first time appointments and/or other appointments as assigned. Assures accurate information is gathered to support clinical and financial needs. Provides support to physicians and consumer by coordinating their requests and satisfying their needs in one phone call. Solves routine and complex customer problems. Communicates regularly with physicians, medical secretaries and staff within the product/service line to ensure customer and department staff needs are met. Displays the highest level of customer service, attentiveness and consideration possible in all cases. Uses integrated health information systems and telecommunication technology and customer service skills to facilitate customer interactions such that the customer experiences the Medical Center and its entities as an accessible, coordinated and seamless entity. Generates system reports and utilizes system reporting tools to demonstrate product line success and/or lack of relative to referrals, access, appointments, wait times. Presents product line/service line information to key audiences such as service line physicians, and other audiences as assigned. Collaborates with these same audiences as necessary for problem resolution. Minimum Qualifications High School diploma or GED. Certification or vocational training may be required. 4 years of relevant experience required. 6 or more years of relevant experience preferred. Bachelor’s Degree preferred and experience in healthcare or physician practice preferred. Medical terminology, ICD-9 diagnosis coding and third party reimbursement experience a plus. Demonstrated ability to work in multiple Databases for management and reporting. Ability to work in self-directed manner while interacting with consumers, physicians and all medical center faculty and staff. Familiarity with OSUMC and its entities preferred. Career Roadmap FUNCTION: Finance SUB-FUNCTION: Revenue Cycle - Scheduling CAREER BAND: Individual Contributor - Technical CAREER LEVEL: T4 Additional Information: Location: Spielman Comprehensive Breast Center (0874) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Planned-and-Preventative-Maintenance-Specialist_R158608-1": {
      "title": "Planned and Preventative Maintenance Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Planned and Preventative Maintenance Specialist Department: Student Life | North Maintenance Job Description Provides coordination and resolution for all facilities related issues to ensure a prescribed level of performance and function for all Student Life areas (~6.2M square feet). Often works autonomously and acts as a first responder, providing oversight, coordinating efforts to ensure an expedient response for facilities issues that arise during weekends, holidays and off hours.  Delivers and executes Student Life planned and preventative maintenance program focused on building, mechanical, and dining related equipment and infrastructure.  Coordinates with Student Life Facilities Managers to support building operations and events; works with other university departments to ensure compliance and safety of exterior amenities. This position will participate in project work consisting of planned replacements, quality assurance, process improvement, and data collection and review; responsible for responding to urgent reactionary service requests of day-to-day facilities related tasks as needed. Supervises and coordinates activities of contractors and university business partners. Hands-on responsibilities include install, repair, replace and maintain building infrastructure components including; plumbing, electrical, mechanical and HVAC related equipment, building envelope, floors, and furniture. Typically transitions from planned and preventative work to reactionary work, based on needs of the operation; receives service requests via CMMS system; attends departmental functions and needed training; will operate departmental vehicles regularly. Schedule The schedule for this position is 9:00 pm - 9:00 am with a rotating schedule that includes working Thursday - Tuesday every other week, including any holidays that fall within the scheduled rotation. Responsibilities 50% Technical Skills: Develops, delivers and executes Student Life planned and preventative maintenance program; identifies and documents deficiencies and corrective measures needed; diagnoses building and mechanical system issues and determines how to resolve or mitigate them; reacts to urgent facilities issues; installs, repairs, replaces, and maintains building, mechanical and dining related equipment and systems, adheres to all safety practices and procedures 30% Leadership: Promotes stewardship of university facilities; responsible for all facilities related activities for assigned periods.  May conduct, supervise, or assist in facilities inspections and provide feedback to appropriate personnel.  Conducts and participates in team meetings, works with line staff and managers for safe work practices measures; creates reports on findings.  Identifies areas and processes that need improvement and provide solutions. Reviews, revises, and manages building/system specific preventive maintenance programs as requested. and program compliance, maintains up-to-date safety manuals and Safety Data Sheets (SDS) documentation. Complies with Operations accountability. Delegates tasks to team members based on operational needs, coordinates efforts with Student Life Facilities managers to support building operations and events, supervises activities and checks for satisfactory project completion, identifies deficiencies in campus facilities and initiates changes that benefit the well-being of campus life, responds to crisis situations in an appropriate manner, and escalates as needed to appropriate departments. 20% Customer Service / Communication; corresponds with contractors and university business partners, provides excellent customer service, frequently communicates with management to acknowledge and respond to emergency situations, ensures timely response and completion of all maintenance requests, follows up on outstanding issues as applicable, documents all completed tasks, maintains presentable appearance.    Qualifications Required: Bachelor’s degree in a related field or equivalent combination of education and experience; 2 years of maintenance experience, must be able to push/pull 70 pounds, climb ladders, valid driver’s license, successful completion of a background check. Desired: 2-4 years of maintenance experience, maintenance certification from a recognized industry board, familiarity with university facilities and operations, 3-5 years of leadership experience, EPA universal certification (section 608). Additional Information: Compensation The targeted pay range for this position is $28.22 - $37.12 based on education and experience. This position is eligible for weekend and evening shift premiums as applicable. Career Roadmap Information Function: Facilities, Engineering and Acquisition Subfunction: Facilities Operations Career Band: Specialized Career Level: 2 Location: Scott House (1108) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Rotating Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Research-Senior-Technician---Comprehensive-Cancer-Center_R149720-1": {
      "title": "Research Senior Technician - Comprehensive Cancer Center",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Research Senior Technician - Comprehensive Cancer Center Department: Medicine | School Biomedical Sciences Molecular Medicine and Therapeutics Summary: Dr. Chandler’s Laboratory, situated within the Ohio State University Comprehensive Cancer Center (OSUCCC) is devoted to understanding how dysregulation of RNA processing contributes to cancer development and therapeutic resistance. Our research centers on defining the mechanisms that control alternative pre‑mRNA splicing of oncogenes, signaling molecules, and immune regulators, and on leveraging these pathways for therapeutic intervention across multiple cancer types, including liver and breast cancer.  Using molecular, genomic, and in vivo approaches, we develop splice‑modulating strategies, such as splice‑switching oligonucleotides, to restore tumor suppressor activity and disrupt oncogenic signaling networks. We're looking for a highly motivated individual to join our team as a Research Senior Technician at OSUCCC. Your role will be pivotal in several significant research projects in Cancer Biology. You'll collaborate closely with the lab staff so strong organizational and communication skills are crucial. Adaptability to new technologies and a fast-paced work environment is a must. You'll also have the opportunity to contribute to major research papers and participate in national and international conferences. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or equivalent experience required; 4 years of relevant experience required with High School diploma or GED, 2 years of relevant experience required with Associate's Degree, or 0 years of relevant experience required with Bachelor's Degree. Ability to translate, adapt and apply academic and/or practical knowledge in the conduct of biological/health science research is required. Experience in a biological/health science research capacity is preferred. Career Roadmap: FUNCTION:  Research SUB-FUNCTION: Research & Scholarship CAREER BAND: Individual Contributor CAREER LEVEL: T3 Additional Information: Location: Pelotonia Research Center (1040) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
