    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Chemical-and-Biomolecular-Engineering---Post-Doctoral-Scholar_R157065": {
      "title": "Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering - Post Doctoral Scholar",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering - Post Doctoral Scholar Department: Engineering | Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering The Ohio State University, College of Engineering, William G. Lowrie Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering is seeking a Post Doctoral Scholar to work under the supervision of Dr. Joseph Kwon. We’re seeking a creative Postdoctoral Scholar to join our team and advance cutting-edge multiscale and hybrid modeling—integrating first-principles simulations with machine learning—for chemical and biological applications. You will design and implement models ranging from molecular to process scales, develop model-predictive control and optimization strategies, run high-performance numerical experiments, analyze data, and communicate your findings through journal publications and conference presentations. The ideal candidate holds a Ph.D. in Chemical Engineering (or a related field), is proficient in both mechanistic modeling and ML frameworks (e.g., TensorFlow, PyTorch), and has strong programming skills (Python/MATLAB/C++). Join us to tackle sustainability and biomanufacturing challenges, mentor students, collaborate across disciplines, and help translate transformative research into real-world impact. Required Education: PhD in Chemical Engineering or related field Required Education: 1 year of prior research experience on multiscale modeling, hybrid modeling, and model-based control or related fields Desired Experience: 3 years of prior research experience on multiscale modeling, hybrid modeling, and model-based control or related fields. Additional Information: Location: CBEC (0248) Position Type: Term (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Harding-Hospital/Staff-Nurse--RN----Adult-Inpatient-Psychiatry_R157438-1": {
      "title": "Staff Nurse (RN) - Young Adult Inpatient Psychiatry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Staff Nurse (RN) - Young Adult Inpatient Psychiatry Department: Harding | 4NP Adult Inpatient Psychiatry Scope of Position: The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center’s mission is to improve health in Ohio and across the world through innovation in research, education, and patient care. The team provides patient care and supportive services directed towards achievement of positive patient care outcomes, maximizing the patient’s involvement in his/her own plan of care and reducing the length of hospitalization, The staff nurse plays a critical role in staff engagement, the patient experience, quality and safety, and cost-effective care. Position Summary: The Staff Nurse is responsible for managing and providing care to the patient and his/her family, and for directing and supervising nursing care provided by other members of the patient care team. The Staff Nurse is responsible for assessing, planning, implementing, coordinating, delegating and evaluating the nursing care of patients in alignment with the professional practice model.  Minimum Qualifications For Hire:   2- year College Degree in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program is required.   Bachelor’s degree in nursing with a major in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program is preferred. Current Ohio license or interim permit required. 2 years of experience in behavioral or acute care setting is preferred. ​ On-going:  Maintains current Ohio RN license. Meets mandatory educational and health requirements.  Demonstrates computer skills required to meet job functions. Additional Information: Harding Hospital at the OSU Wexner Medical Center offers adult and geriatric in-patient program with 84 beds and provides emergency stabilization, diagnosis and the initial stages of treatment for those requiring inpatient care. Patient-centered, trauma-informed care is supported by an interdisciplinary team with a strong focus on staff and patient safety, clinical excellence, and professional growth. Harding 4th floor is an 18-bed psychiatric behavioral health unit at Harding Hospital specializing in treating a wide range of mental health conditions, with particular expertise in suicidal ideation, mood disorders, and anxiety. This position is full time varying shift. Candidates should be open to working both days and nights based on patient need. Location: Harding Hospital (0165) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 36 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Operations-Analyst_R158191-1": {
      "title": "Operations Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Operations Analyst Department: Academic Affairs Administration | Salmon P. Chase Center for Civics, Culture, and Society Salmon P. Chase Center for Civics, Culture, and Society The Ohio State University’s motto, Disciplina in Civitatem, or “education for citizenship,” is not merely a slogan; it is an exhortation to remain focused on the responsibility to develop an informed, engaged, and civic-minded citizenry. It is essential to fulfilling Ohio State’s land-grant mission.   The Salmon P. Chase Center is a multidisciplinary university center that conducts teaching, research, and public programming concerning the core texts and great debates of Western civilization; the principles, ideals, and institutions of the American and Ohio political order; and the foundations of responsible leadership and informed citizenship. It is an independent academic unit of the University. The Center is a leader of the growing cadre of similar centers of civic thought and leadership in Ohio and throughout the country.   POSITION OVERVIEW: The Salmon P. Chase Center for Civics, Culture, and Society is conducting a search for an Operations Analyst who will support the Center’s day-to-day operations. The Operations Analyst will work closely with the Center’s Operations Manager to develop and maintain best practices for business and program administration. The Operations Analyst will oversee numerous business processes; coordinate  course administration; serve as an administrative resource to faculty; and manage the Center’s facilities. The Operations Analyst will enable the Center’s continued growth as the flourishing academic community envisioned in ORC § 3335.39. The Operations Analyst, as with all members of the Center, should embrace the Center’s mission.   Financial Administration, Purchasing, and Travel The Operations Analyst oversees the Center’s individual spending accounts, including faculty research and start-up, managing their budgets, reconciling transactions, analyzing spending, and producing monthly reports.   The Operations Analyst manages the Center’s budgets for various student programs and initiatives, developing practices for tracking expenses and communicating with faculty and staff to ensure compliance with policies and procedures.     The Operations Analyst independently manages all domestic and international travel for faculty and staff. Required Qualifications: Demonstrated commitment to the Chase Center’s mission of citizenship education. Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience. 2 years of relevant experience. Demonstrated poise, professionalism, good judgment, and ability to take the extra step to meet customer needs.   Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team Strong organizational skills and attention to detail   Ability to work in a fast-paced, changing environment, and manage multiple projects simultaneously. Regular in-person attendance is expected.     Desired Qualifications: 2-4 years of relevant experience. Familiarity with university policies and procedures.   The Operations Analyst coordinates purchasing of equipment, supplies, and services and processes procurement and payments in compliance with university and Center policies and procedures.   The Operations Analyst works with the Operations Manager to develop, implement, and maintain the Center’s business processes.    Program Support The Operations Analyst works with the Center’s Associate Director and faculty administrators to develop and maintain the Center’s course schedules.   The Operations Analyst manages course, enrollment, and teaching data, producing regular reports. Working with the Operations Manager, the Operations Analyst develops enrollment dashboards and analyzes relevant data.   The Operations Analyst coordinates coursebook orders and secures instructor desk copies.   Facilities Management The Operations Analyst manages the Center’s facilities, coordinating maintenance and service requests and ensuring good stewardship of the Center’s space and assets.   The Operations Analyst manages building access and brass keys.   The Operations Analyst serves as the Center’s liaison to the Office of Technology and Digital Innovation, coordinating support and service for the Center’s resources.   The Operations Analyst assists the Operations Manager with logistical, administrative, and practical tasks related to the maintenance and oversight of the Chase Center’s facilities.   Additional Information: Please submit both a cover letter and a resume to be considered for this opportunity. The Targeted Hiring Range for this position is $55,700 - $68,000 .  The actual salary paid to an individual will vary based on multiple factors, including but not limited to, education, years of experience, internal equity, etc. Function: Business Planning and Operations Subfunction: Business Operations Band: Specialized Level: 2 Location: Page Hall (0061) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Assistant-Director--Student-Athlete-Support-Services-Office--SASSO-_R158455-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student-Athlete Support Services Office (SASSO)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Assistant Director, Student-Athlete Support Services Office (SASSO) Department: Undergraduate Education | Student Athlete Support Services The Assistant Director in Student-Athlete Support Services Office (SASSO) within the Office of Student Academic Success manages the learning and instruction specifically around strategies for academic success for the under prepared and underrepresented student-athletes. Identifies student-athletes skill set for college level work. Designs and implements strategic instructional plans for student-athletes under-prepared for college. Engages in small groups and individuals in implementation of instructional plans. Analyzes effectiveness of program and recommends improvements, directs implementations and coordinates new strategies to ensure continuous improvement. Develops and implements learning interventions and study strategies in the areas of time management, critical thinking, reading and writing, taking notes, test taking, etc. Works from a developmental perspective, meeting the student where they are, recognizing the needs of each student, and working with a problem solving focus. Collaborates with educational services team members to create programming that will aid in the preparation for exams. This includes but is not limited to review and prep sessions for a variety of courses, trainings for tutors and other SASSO initiatives/projects. This position is focused on the holistic development of a student-athlete's well-being: personal, academic, involvement, and professional development. The Assistant Director manages a team of full time staff members. Manages and creates professional development opportunities for SASSO staff. Manages a caseload of student-athletes on a daily basis, including coaching, feedback and addresses performance concerns as needed. Performs other SASSO special projects and duties as assigned. Additional Information: Required Qualifications : Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of experience and education is required. Five (5) years experience required. Experience with postsecondary students. Desired Qualifications : Master's degree. Eight to twelve ( 8-12) years of relevant experience preferred. Familiarity with NCAA, Big Ten Conference and OSU rules and regulations. Supervisory experience. experience advising/tutoring/mentoring collegiate student-athletes or previous experience teaching at the collegiate. Experience developing and motivating students for athletic and academic success. To apply, submit a current resume and cover letter describing your interest and related experience for this position. The pay range for this job profile is $58,700 - $74,000. The offer for this position will fall withing this range based on internal equity, unit's available budget, and the candidate's qualifications. Job profile: Student-Athlete Services Manager 2 Function: Athletics Sub-function: Student-Athlete Services Career Band: People Leader Career Level: M2 Location: Younkin Success Center (0052) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Remote-Location/Senior-Project-Manager_R158249-1": {
      "title": "Senior Project Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Senior Project Manager Department: Nursing | College Administration The Senior Project Manager provides dedicated project management oversight, administration coordination, and trainee support for the MOHERE (Master's in One Health and Emergency Research Ethics) project and its associated grant activities. The Senior Project Manager fosters collaboration among internal and external partners including the international subawardee, the University of Nairobi, Kenya, to facilitate project deliverables. Key responsibilities include overseeing project planning, resourcing, budgeting, invoicing, and progress reporting; ensuring deliverables meet quality and cost standards; and monitoring project status. Additionally, this role serves as the primary administrative point of contact for the MOHERE PI and key investigators, overseeing MOHERE team communications, tracking trainee progress, designing and distributing evaluation surveys, and organizing workshops and program events.  Key responsibilities include: Overseeing overall grant administration, timeline tracking, and compliance for the MOHERE project. Leading trainee-facing operations, including overseeing scholarship appointments, ongoing communications, cohort tracking, and feedback collection. Supporting key project planning activities, co-ordinating team meetings, compiling progress reports, managing project calendars, and coordinating domestic and international travel for PI and key personnel. Initiating Workday transactions (requisitions, spend authorizations, expense reports, and reimbursements) Developing presentations, spreadsheets and briefing materials for internal and external project stakeholders. Coordinating logistics for annual workshops, training modules, and special events. Additional Information: Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. Advanced degree in relevant field may be desired. 4 years of relevant experience required. 4-8 years of relevant experience preferred. Position funding ends March 31, 2027. Applications will be accepted through September 9, 2026. Function: Business Planning and Operations Sub-function: Project Management Career Band: Individual Contributor - Specialized Career Level: S3 Salary range: $81,800 - $106,900 Location: Remote Location Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 32 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
