    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Companion-Animal-Registered-Veterinary-Technician--RVT--Opportunities_R152205": {
      "title": "Companion Animal Registered Veterinary Technician (RVT) Opportunities",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Companion Animal Registered Veterinary Technician (RVT) Opportunities Department: Veterinary Medical Center | Operations S hift differential (up to $2.50/hour) and weekend differential (up to $4.50/hour), as well as overtime and compensatory time eligible.    S pecialty Care Veterinary Technician (RVT) for dogs and cats        Become an integral part of a renowned academic institution where you will utilize  your advanced training and skills, to help provide world-class medical care to patients of The Ohio State University Veterinary Medical Center hospitals!        Our  Hummel-Trueman H o spital for Companion Animals  clinical teams provide exceptional and comprehensive  spe c ialty care  for dogs and cats, while also providing unmatched, “aha!” learning experiences for our veterinary students.  You will be helping to teach tomorrow's general practitioners and veterinary specialists, while performing at the top of your licensure.   Never a dull moment here!       Like human medicine, our advanced specialty veterinary care services include, but are not limited to, anesthesia, cardiology, diagnostic imaging, emergency critical care, internal medicine, neurology, oncology, ophthalmology, and several others.  Find what inspires you!      Enjoy  opportunities for growth and development , including support and mentoring from our Staff Education Coordinator for technicians interested in pursuing VTS certification.    In addition, we offer these  exceptional benefits :    Access to extensive free Continuing Education Resources and annual CE Allowance   Uniform allowance    Support of technician VTS/specialization processes    An array of retirement plan options, each with generous employer contributions    Competitive Vacation and Sick Leave Program including paid parental leave.     11 Paid Holidays per year    Affordable Medical Insurance, Dental and Vision Insurance that begins on day one.    Lifestyle Spending Account     OSU tuition benefit for you and your dependents    Priority access to purchase season tickets to OSU sporting events      Required Education     Associate  degree in animal health/veterinary medicine    Completed and successfully passed VTNE prior to hire date.     State of Ohio Registered Veterinary Technician at the time of hire.          RVT experience including a combination of RVT and Veterinary Assistant a plus!   Opportunities include – Veterinary Care Tech 2 for the following specialties: Hiring Range $23.89 - $29.86 Behavior Cardiology Dermatology Hospital Patient Care Internal medicine Neurology Oncology Rehabilitation Ophthalmology Surgery (Both Soft Tissue and Orthopedic) Veterinary Care Tech 3 for the following specialties: Hiring Range $28.22 - $35.29 Anesthesia Emergency/Critical Care   Apply today and we will follow up with you to find your best next experience!    Additional Information: Location: Veterinary Medical Center (0299) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
