    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Collection-Curator-and-Archivist_R157792-1": {
      "title": "Collection Curator and Archivist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Collection Curator and Archivist Department: Undergraduate Education | Frank W. Hale, Jr. Black Cultural Center The Hale Black Cultural Center seeks a strategically minded professional to lead the stewardship, development, and activation of its African American art collection. In alignment with the Office of Academic Affairs’ directive, this role will strengthen the connection between HBCC’s mission and the collection by improving digital and physical accessibility, expanding community engagement, and elevating the visibility of the works through programming, partnerships, and scholarship. The position serves as the primary collection advocate—supporting archival infrastructure, building donor and artist relationships, coordinating collection-centered events, and representing the cultural and historical significance of the archive within the university and broader community. Required education Bachelor's degree and 4+ years of experience Required Qualifications Demonstrated knowledge of art handling, preservation, archival or museum collection methods. Ability to communicate the cultural significance of a collection to diverse audiences. Experience with databases, metadata, or digital archiving systems. Ability to manage interns, student staff, or volunteers. Strong writing skills, especially for catalogue entries, interpretive material, or grant proposals. Experience with cultural or arts-based programming and/or community organizing. Knowledge of African American art history or cultural heritage work. Preferred Qualifications Grant writing and/or fundraising experience. Experience with oral histories, community-based archives, or culturally rooted collections. Experience working with artists, donors, families, or estates. Experience designing collection-based programs or exhibitions. Familiarity with university arts infrastructure or cultural center operations. The Hale Black Cultural Center seeks a visionary, detail-oriented collection steward who can protect and grow the HBCC art archive while ensuring its cultural, academic, and community significance is fully realized. This role will build archival infrastructure, nurture donor and artist relationships, develop collection-centered programming, and serve as a primary public representative of the collection’s relevance within the university and beyond. This is a full-time, limited-term appointment of two years , with the possibility of a one-year extension (maximum three years total) based on exceptional performance and departmental needs.  Additional Information: Please submit both a cover letter and a resume to be considered for this opportunity. The target hiring range for this job profile is $ 47,700 - $66,000 The actual salary paid to an individual will vary based on multiple factors, including but not limited to, education, years of experience, internal equity, etc.  Location: Hale Hall (0085) Position Type: Term (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
