    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-Hospital/Staff-Nurse-B_R152974-1": {
      "title": "Staff Nurse (RN)- NICU",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Staff Nurse (RN)- NICU Department: University Hospital | Neonatal Intensive Care Unit Job Description Scope of Position: The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center’s mission is to improve health in Ohio and across the world through innovation in research, education, and patient care. The team provides patient care and supportive services directed towards achievement of positive patient care outcomes, maximizing the patient’s involvement in his/her own plan of care and reducing the length of hospitalization, The staff nurse plays a critical role in staff engagement , the patient experience, quality and safety, and cost effective care. Position Summary: The Staff Nurse is responsible for managing and providing care to the patient and his/her family, and for directing and supervising nursing care provided by other members of the patient care team. The Staff Nurse is responsible for assessing, planning, implementing, coordinating, delegating and evaluating the nursing care of patients in alignment with the professional practice model. Required Qualifications Degree in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program required. Current Ohio license or interim permit. *Experience in relevant care setting preferred. Additional Information: Additional Job Description The Nationwide Children's NICU at The University Hospital Wexner Medical Center is a 51 bed, Level III Neonatal Intensive Care Unit. Our NICU team includes a variety of team members including nurses, PCAS, UCAs, milk techs, who work directly with an even larger multi-disciplinary team from Physicians, to NNPs, Case Managers, Nutrition, Pharmacy and Social Workers, specifically dedicated to our NICU population. As a Nationwide Children's NICU here at OSU, we are a part of the NCH Neonatal Network making us one of ten NICU throughout the city. Location: University Hospital (0870) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 36 Shift: Third Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-Hospital/Surgical-Technologist---Inpatient-2_R157237-1": {
      "title": "Surgical Technologist - University Hospital",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Surgical Technologist - University Hospital Department: University Hospital | Operating Room Scope/Position Summary The ST performs technical skills related to interoperative patient care.  The ST is generally assigned to perform the scrub role in various surgical procedures and also performs routine unit tasks.  They provide emergency care measures as appropriate, and assist in meeting the patient's emotional needs.  The ST follows universal precautions, safe handling guidelines, and all other infection control standards.  They provide for safety/security of self and others and follow special precautions as related to patient care.  They maintain a clean/organized perioperative unit.  The ST promotes a positive attitude to staff, families, and patient/guests as well as maintains patient confidentiality.  The ST is an unclassified professional staff position working under direct supervision of PCC-RN and under the general supervision of perioperative Managers.  The ST performs all tasks in a manner that is cost effective without compromising quality of care, meets hospital continuing education and certification  requirements, upholds goals and objectives of the Department of Per i operative Services.  The ST contributes to organizational effectiveness and demonstrates career growth a development. The ST works variable rotating shifts as assigned.  Call is assigned on a rotating basis. Minimum Qualifications Must be a high school graduate or possess the GED, and must have completed formal Surgical Technology Training Program.  Previous experience in the Operating Room as Surgical Technologist is preferred. Additional Information: Location: University Hospital - Doan Hall (0089) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Program-Coordinator_R158133-1": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Program Coordinator Department: Undergraduate Education | Frank W. Hale, Jr. Black Cultural Center Leads outreach, communications, programming coordination, and student engagement initiatives for HBCC. This role supports the development, promotion, and implementation of programs and events while fostering relationships with students, campus partners, artists, and community collaborators. The position also contributes to operational coordination, marketing efforts, and student-facing initiatives that enhance visibility, engagement, and participation across HBCC programming. Primary Responsibilities Programming, Events & Cultural Engagement Manage the planning, coordination, implementation, and assessment of HBCC programs, events, and initiatives Lead the event logistics, scheduling, registration systems, and operational coordination Maintain and initiate communication and logistics with vendors, collaborators, speakers, performers, and campus/community partners Lead hospitality, setup, breakdown, and other event-related operational needs Manage maintaining organizational systems, calendars, timelines, and event documentation Support gallery programming, exhibitions, artist engagement, and collection-centered initiatives Create and administer educational, cultural, and creative programming connected to HBCC collections and spaces Coordinate logistics and communication related to exhibitions, installations, and cultural events Support visitor engagement and community participation related to collections programming Marketing, Communications & Outreach Manage marketing, communications, and promotional efforts for HBCC programs and initiatives Maintain with social media coordination, digital engagement, and content scheduling Coordinate listserv messaging, reminder communications, and outreach campaigns Collaborate with university marketing and communications partners as needed Manage development of promotional materials, visibility initiatives, and audience engagement strategies Assist with maintaining consistent communication practices and public-facing messaging Manage outreach, engagement, and visibility initiatives that strengthen HBCC’s campus and community presence Assist with partnership development, collaborative programming, and community engagement opportunities Build and maintain collaborative relationships with students, departments, student organizations, artists, and community partners Student, Staff & Organizational Support Manage with coordination, onboarding, scheduling, training, and support of student workers and program staff Manage hiring and administrative processes related to graduate assistants, FWS students, interns, and volunteers Maintain student staffing schedules, operational coverage, and communication systems Contribute to creating positive and organized student-facing work environments Participate in collaborative initiatives and other departmental activities as needed Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience 2 years in experience Desired Qualifications 2–4 years’ experience in outreach and engagement, Marketing and student engagement. Additional Information: Please submit both a cover letter and a resume to be considered for this opportunity.   The target hiring range for this job profile is  $ $47,700 - $62,220 The actual salary paid to an individual will vary based on multiple factors, including but not limited to, education, years of experience, internal equity, etc.  Function -   Business Planning and Operations Sub Function -   Community Outreach Band -   Individual Contributor - Specialized Level -   S2 Location: Hale Hall (0085) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Curatorial-Assistant_R157185-2": {
      "title": "Curatorial Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Curatorial Assistant Department: Wexner Center for Arts | Administration The Wexner Center for the Arts at The Ohio State University is an internationally recognized multidisciplinary contemporary arts center dedicated to supporting artistic innovation, experimentation, and public engagement. Through exhibitions, performances, artist residencies, film, education, and public programs, the Wexner Center serves as a laboratory for the exploration of contemporary culture and ideas. The Center is committed to fostering meaningful connections between artists, students, scholars, and the broader community. Position Summary The Curatorial Assistant is an important member of the Visual Arts department, providing research, exhibition, project management, and administrative support to the curatorial team. This position offers an exceptional opportunity for an emerging museum professional to gain broad experience in the development and realization of ambitious contemporary art exhibitions, publications, commissions, and public programs. The ideal candidate will be highly organized, intellectually curious, detail-oriented, and passionate about contemporary art. They will possess excellent research, writing, communication, and project management skills, along with the ability to manage multiple long-term and short-term projects simultaneously. This is a full-time, limited-term appointment of two years , with the possibility of a one-year extension (maximum three years total) based on exceptional performance and departmental needs. The position includes a six-month probationary period . Monday-Friday, with occasional evening and weekend hours required for exhibition openings, public programs, installations, and special events Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree in Art History, Curatorial Studies, Museum Studies, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and professional experience. 0-2 years of relevant experience Demonstrated knowledge of modern and contemporary art. Strong research, writing, editing, and organizational skills. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously while maintaining exceptional attention to detail. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and collaborative project-management tools. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a fast-paced environment. Preferred Master's degree in Art History, Curatorial Studies, Museum Studies, Prior museum, gallery, non-profit arts organization, or academic curatorial experience. Experience supporting contemporary art exhibitions, publications, or artist commissions. Familiarity with collections management or exhibition databases. Experience working with artists, galleries, lenders, and arts professionals. Knowledge of current issues and discourse in contemporary art and curatorial practice. Experience writing for both scholarly and public audiences. Physical Requirements Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this position. Ability to work at a computer for extended periods. Ability to move throughout galleries, offices, storage areas, and event spaces. Occasional lifting, carrying, or moving of materials up to 25 pounds. Occasional evening and weekend work required. Compensation and Benefits The Curatorial Assistant is a full-time benefits-eligible position through The Ohio State University. Salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Eligible employees receive access to university benefits, including health insurance, retirement programs, paid time off, professional development opportunities, and other university-supported resources. Application Process Applicants should submit: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae or Resume Writing Sample (5-10 pages preferred) Contact information for three professional references The Wexner Center for the Arts and The Ohio State University encourage applications from individuals whose experiences and perspectives will contribute to the vitality and excellence of the institution. Additional Information: Position is a member of the American Federation of State, County, & Municipal Employees Local 322, Ohio Council 8, AFL-CIO. The target hourly range for this job profile is $21.55-$27.50. The actual salary paid to an individual will vary based on multiple factors, including but not limited to, education, years of experience, internal equity, etc.  Location: Wexner Center for the Arts (0386) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Security-Information-Analyst_R158448-1": {
      "title": "Security Information Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Security Information Analyst Department: Administration and Planning | DPS Communication and Central Alarm Center Job Description Monitors CCTV cameras, security systems and surveillance equipment for alarms, intrusions, and suspicious actions. Verifies security and safety of University buildings, grounds and property through equipment and protective devices and ensures that these are protected against damage, loss, fire, sabotage, and theft. Reports equipment malfunctions, water leaks, evidence of breaking and entering or equipment damage and other conditions requiring attention. Monitors intrusion detection equipment and maintains communication with Communications Center and other security and law enforcement personnel. Reports and assists in investigation of fires, crimes, unusual incidents, complaints, injuries, accidents or suspicious and unauthorized personnel. Minimum Education Required Per Classified Civil Svc Specs Additional Education Desired HS Graduate or Equivalent or equivalent combination of education and experience Required Qualifications High school graduate or an equivalent amount of education and experience; requires successful completion of background investigation; ability to type and operate a computer terminal; ability to read and write common vocabulary; experience communicating effectively with department, university and non- university personnel strongly desired. Hours and days may vary. Subject to 24-hour call in. This position is identified as an Essential position, whose presence is required regardless of the existence of an emergency condition, and whose absence from duty could endanger the safety and well-being of the campus population and/or physical plant.   Additional Information: Hourly rate is $26.25 per hour If you work a shift from 3pm to 7am, there will be a Shift Differential of $1.25 per hour. Location: Blankenship Hall (0360) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
