    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Coordinator--Student-Governments_R158205-1": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Student Governments",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Coordinator, Student Governments Department: Student Life | Student Activities Administration Coordinator of Student Governments Job Description Details: The Coordinator of Student Governments is a key staff member of the Student Life Ohio Union and Student Activities team. This role serves as the secondary advisor to the Council of Graduate Students and the Inter-Professional Council and provides programming support for the Undergraduate Student Government. This includes meeting regularly with executive officers, directors, and project leads to identify needs and assist students with the implementation of various initiatives and events. As a Student Life staff liaison for the student governments, this role will conduct officer trainings and transitions, officer hiring and timesheet management, event planning, assessment, and approvals, and logistical support for major events. Additionally, this role will serve as a project manager for various events and collaborations, working in partnership with the Sr. Assistant Director, Financial Operations Associate, and student leaders. This role will report to the Sr. Assistant Director for Student Organizations and Student Governments. This role will be an engaged member of the Ohio Union and Student Activities team by attending regular staff meetings and professional development, supporting Student Activities/ Student Life/ university programs as requested, serving on university committees, and other duties as assigned. Duties: 45% - Serve as the secondary advisor to the Council of Graduate Students, the Undergraduate Student Government and Inter-Professional Council; assist executive officers with communications, trainings, officer transitions, budget planning, grant processes, purchasing approvals, and event planning/on-site support for major activities of each organization, including the CGS Hayes Graduate Research Forum, Buckeye Road Trip, and IPC Inter-Professional Summit. This role is also responsible for hiring and timesheet tracking of the paid student leader positions. 45% - Work closely with Student Government leaders in the executive and legislative branches to assist them with event planning and logistics, maintaining a project management structure that will organize priorities for the student government support team; meet regularly with support team to strategize the most effective means for support of student government initiatives; work with the Financial Operations Specialist to educate student government leaders on purchasing and event planning procedures; provide on-site support for student government programs and collaborative events as needed. 10% - Participate in Ohio Union and Student Activities staff meetings and professional development activities, provide support for unit, division, and university programs as needed, serve on university committees, and perform other duties as assigned. Required: Bachelor's degree; two years of relevant work experience; experience working with students in a higher education setting; experience managing multifaceted projects; planning, organizing, and implementation skills; coaching and facilitation skills; and proficiency with Microsoft Office. Desired: Master's degree in higher education and student affairs or related field; experience working with student governments and student leadership development. Salary: The pay rate for this position is $ 22.60 . This is a non-exempt, hourly position that is eligible for overtime. Additional information: Remote work opportunities may be available to facilitate relocation to the Columbus area. Hybrid work opportunities may be available throughout the year as aligned with department goals and programming needs. Additional Information: CRM information: FUNCTION: Student Life, SUB-FUNCTION: Student Leadership, Engagement and Activities, CAREER BAND: Individual Contributor, CAREER LEVEL: Student Leadership, Engagement and Activities Specialist 2. MISSION The Office of Student Life fosters students’ development, learning, well-being and sense of belonging; empowers students to achieve their academic, personal and professional goals; and prepares students to be engaged in a global society.  Ohio State will not sponsor applicants for work visas for this position Location: Ohio Union (0161) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Health-System-Shared-Services/Accounting-Manager_R156164-1": {
      "title": "Accounting Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Accounting Manager Department: Health System Shared Services | General Accounting and Reimbursement Job Description The Accounting Manager provides financial reporting and analysis to all business units and departments within The Ohio State University Health System. The position ensures the month and year end financial statement close schedule/process is maintained. Working with the Accounting leadership, manages the day-to-day operations and business processes of an accounting team. Monitors proper recording of OSUP financial transactions, assets, liabilities, revenue, and expenses in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP) and following Governmental Accounting Standards Board (GASB) guidance. Oversees the maintenance and reconciliation of general ledger accounts. Assists with month, quarter, and year end close activities. Implements process improvement activities in accounting business processes. Assists in development, training, and performance management of accounting team members. This position manages the processes in the general ledger, maintenance of accurate and reconciled accounts, and for accurate financial reporting at a cost center and business unit level. The Manager supervises staff responsible for the reconciliation of accounts and is accountable for the overall accuracy of journal entries to ensure the general ledger is in accordance with accounting principles and reporting schedules so that the organization has a full and accurate statement of its financial position. This position assists in strategic reporting as it relates to the Health System and Medical Center initiatives. The Manager performs as a subject matter expert when identified as a resource required for projects and strategic requests and acts as key a resource for financial and operational management, product line committees, operational improvement teams, and strategic initiatives. This position is responsible for accounting projects involving high business risk, scope and impact to the organization. This position is recognized across the organization for expertise and sought as a source for resolution of unique or the most complex financial problems. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field required; advanced degree and CPA strongly preferred. Minimum of five years of accounting experience, preferably in a healthcare environment. Strong knowledge of accounting principles, financial analysis, budgeting, forecasting, and regulatory requirements. Demonstrated leadership experience, proficiency with spreadsheets and project management software, understanding of industry trends, and application of lean or continuous improvement principles. Additional Information: Our Comprehensive Employee Benefits Include: An array of retirement plan options, each with a generous employer contribution. Affordable health insurance options, including dental, vision and prescription coverage that begin on day one. Paid vacation and sick leave, including short and long-term disability and paid parental leave. Get the most out of the Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. And much more! Location: Ackerman Rd, 660 (0242) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
