    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Global-Programs-Coordinator_R153808-1": {
      "title": "Global Programs Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Global Programs Coordinator Department: Veterinary Medicine | Veterinary Preventive Medicine The College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) is seeking a Program Coordinator to assist with the management and daily operations of select global programs, including the Global Engagement Program and an extramurally funded award related to global veterinary education and capacity building. The Program Coordinator would be expected to contribute to general administrative assistance including travel and event planning, expense reporting, receiving/tracking/submitting invoices, ensuring compliance with university and sponsor standards, preparation of written reports (technical reports/bulletins, press releases, annual reports) and audiovisual materials (PowerPoint presentations, online content), inventory management for project supplies, meeting scheduling and communications with internal (university) and external partners, and data management. The coordinator would work closely with faculty investigators and other staff/students to facilitate efficient and effective execution of program activities. Additionally, the coordinator may work with government entities and international (overseas) partners to facilitate activities abroad. Physical Requirements: Sitting/standing at a desk, computer use for long periods of time (6-8 hrs/day)  . International or domestic travel is not a requirement but may be possible with this position . Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma or GED; 4 years of relevant experience or equivalent education/experience (e.g., Bachelor’s degree). Computer literacy, including proficiency with Microsoft Office suite (Word, PowerPoint, Excel). Strong written and oral communication skills. High attention to detail and accuracy. Strong project and time management skills. Desired Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree with a Major in communications, business, education, health sciences, international affairs, or other related disciplines. Previous experience in a higher education / university setting. Experience using Workday. Experience writing in a science-based field. International programs administration. Cultural competency. Interest or experience in website editing and/or graphic design. Additional Information: Target Salary Range: $18.37 - $23.99 per hour ; commensurate with experience, internal equity, the unit’s available budget, and the candidate’s qualifications. Location: Sisson Hall (0080) Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
