    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Health-System-Shared-Services/Financial-Acct-Analyst-Med-Ctr_R155533-1": {
      "title": "Financial Acct Analyst-Med Ctr",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Financial Acct Analyst-Med Ctr Department: CCC | Administrative Office Summary: Financial Analyst provides support to Senior Financial Analysts and Finance Manager in overseeing a wide variety of OSU funds within the OSU Comprehensive Cancer Center (OSUCCC): performs monthly analysis and reconciliation of funds; prepares monthly reports and provides financial statements to the Faculty, OSUCCC Finance Manager, and Senior Administrative Staff; alerts Senior Financial Analysts and Finance Manager of discrepancies, errors, and non-compliance to fund expenditures; initiates journal transactions; initiates deposit journals; monitors fund balances to alert Senior Financial Analyst of potential deficits or problems; reviews, reconciles and verifies necessary backup documentation and that appropriate approvals have been received for all supply, service, and equipment expenditures; Performs analysis of budget to actual data on monthly, quarterly, and annual bases for fund financial review and forecasting; monitors accounting practices assuring compliance with audit standards; provides information on OSU and OSUCCC departmental fiscal policies and procedures; works with Purchasing to resolve procurement issues with vendors or other departments, utilizes University’s HR, Financial, and Procurement systems to manage information; performs random sample internal audits of financial transactions including travel, pcard, purchase orders, and reimbursements; maintains fiscal records and files; participates in year-end account closing activities; works directly with the OSUCCC supported Faculty to provide support in financial management, budgeting, fund analysis, reporting and other financial services as needed; processes, performs other financial and accounting duties as assigned.   Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or other Business related field required, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. 2 years of relevant experience required. 2-4 years of relevant experience preferred. Proficiency in Microsoft Excel is required. Knowledge of a general ledger system is desirable. Requires successful completion of a background check; qualified candidates may be asked to complete a pre-employment physical, including a drug screen. Additional Information: Location: Ackerman Rd, 650 (0241) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Senior-Project-Manager-Utility-Program-Integration--ENGIE-_R157768-1": {
      "title": "Senior Project Manager-Utility Program Integration (ENGIE)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Senior Project Manager-Utility Program Integration (ENGIE) Department: Administration and Planning | Facilities, Design and Construction Serves as the primary university liaison responsible for ensuring coordination and integration of ENGIE (utility concessionaire) capital improvement and energy projects with university stakeholders, and ensuring alignment with university planning (PARE), active projects (FDC), and ongoing operations (FOD) and alignment with the Energy Office in Office of Business and Finance. This role provides program-level oversight and coordination for a portfolio of ENGIE-led projects, ensuring successful integration with the university.  ENGIE retains responsibility for project delivery; this position ensures alignment, coordination, and issue resolution across all stakeholders. Provides guidance and mentorship to FDC Project Managers managing projects that include ENGIE scope and ensures alignment with FDC projects and ENGIE scope. ENGIE Program Coordination & Integration Serves as the primary point of contact for Capital Projects between ENGIE and the university Ensures ENGIE projects are coordinated with the Energy Office, campus stakeholders, FOD Operations, and university units Ensures alignment with university standards, master planning, and operational constraints.  Will influence changes to the standards as needed. Involvement in Energy Advisory Committee, review of utility capital plan and 5-year plan including but not limited to committees integral to this role.  Identifies and resolves conflicts between ENGIE and university capital projects Identifies and proactively coordinates university projects with ENGIE. Portfolio Oversight (Non-Delivery Role) Provides program-level coordination and oversight of ENGIE project portfolio Ensures alignment across multiple concurrent projects and proactively communicates and ensure accountability for all related projects.  Advises schedules, outages, and campus impacts if University responsibility but has high communication if Engie is responsible.  ENGIE maintains responsibility for project delivery in most cases, should ENGIE provide funding to the University the University will coordinate the project delivery in accordance with project requirements.  Stakeholder Engagement & Communication Ensure projects are coordinated by ENGIE and appropriate stakeholders are identified unless the university is the responsible party to deliver Assists in communicating impacts such as outages and disruptions unless OSU is delivering projects. Provides updates to leadership and stakeholders Support & Mentorship Guides FDC PMs on projects involving ENGIE Develops coordination standards and best practices, continuously looks for improvement opportunities when working with ENGIE.  Assists with integration, scheduling, and issue resolution Construction Coordination Counsels ENGIE on construction activities regarding campus activities (events, CABS routes, academic calendar, etc.) Resolves access, outage, and phasing conflicts Ensures proactive communication with university leadership and stakeholders Compliance & Standards Ensures projects align with university standards, university project management software, and regulations Ensures close alignment with ENGIE master plan, estimating, projected costs and actively looks for ways to improve processes. Documentation & Reporting Maintains coordination documentation Provides reporting on risks, schedules, and impacts Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience; 4 years in capital project management or construction; experience coordinating complex programs.  4-8 years of relevant experience/ Engineering background preferred. Additional Information: The target hiring range for this job profile is $88,300 - $115,350 annually. The actual salary paid to an individual will vary based on multiple factors, including but not limited to, education, years of experience, internal equity, etc. Function - Facilities, Engineering and Acquisition Sub Function - Facilities Project Management Band - Individual Contributor Level - S3 Location: Enarson Classroom Building (0072) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-Hospital/Occupational-Therapist_R153624-2": {
      "title": "Occupational Therapist (OT) Acute Inpatient",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Occupational Therapist (OT) Acute Inpatient Department: University Hospital | Rehabilitation Services, Acute Care The Occupational Therapist evaluates and treats patients in accordance with the laws and rules that govern the practice of occupational therapy in the state of Ohio. The patient populations an occupational therapist on this team will serve, but is not limited to, general medicine and general surgery, burn patients, patients within the observation and ED units, postpartum, critical care, ortho-trauma, geriatrics and long-term care. Although team members report directly to a team leader, they are also responsible to each other, to those they supervise, and to other participants included in the patient care activities. Minimum Qualifications Masters Level Degree or equivalent combination of education and experience with a Major in Occupational therapy. All rehabilitation team members must be licensed or certified with the respective profession. Occupational therapy must meet the educational and/or certification requirements established by their professions. Occupational therapists must hold a Master's degree. All academic degrees must have been granted by an accredited institution. Additional Information: Location: University Hospital (0870) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Dental-Assistant_R155796-1": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant & Mobile Clinic Driver",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Dental Assistant & Mobile Clinic Driver Department: Dentistry | Dental Public Health The Ohio State University College of Dentistry seeks a Dental Assistant (DA) who will share the responsibility of driving the mobile dental clinic (Dental H.O.M.E. Coach) for The Ohio State University College of Dentistry’s Office of Community Education in the Division of Dental Public Health. The successful candidate will be responsible for direct chair-side dental assisting for all faculty, residents and students in the Dental H.O.M.E. Coach for the College of Dentistry, including assisting with children and special needs patients. Responsibilities Include: Dispenses, receives, and processes instruments, equipment and supplies used in the delivery of treatment Stocks clinic supplies for the clinical area Rotates stock, maintains supply inventory, which includes moving materials, pushing and pulling carts, lifting small equipment, stooping, climbing up and down vehicle stairs Provides oral hygiene instructions, ensures efficient coach operation during clinical sessions Organizes records system Offers a systematic and streamline approach to the delivery of care to patients at various locations, and takes radiographs on young and adult patients Assists Coach Manager with scheduling, logistics, and communication with community partners to support mobile clinic operations Provides regular updates on clinic activities and operational issues. This position requires a valid CDL driver’s license, successful completion of background check(s) and drug & alcohol screening, and the individual is subject to random drug screening per CDL regulations. Work Schedule : The core hours of the College of Dentistry are Monday through Friday, 7:30 am – 4:30 pm. Hours may vary based on needs and may include weekend and/or evening work. Overnight travel may be required when providing services at distant locations. Hiring Range: The targeted hiring pay range is $20 .24 to $26.44 based on experience and education. A 10% pay allowance is provided when the individual is actively driving the Coach. Physical Requirements: A dental assistant needs to have use of both hands, as well as dexterity in the fingers and the ability to manipulate instruments, materials, dental hand pieces, and operate dental equipment. The use of feet is necessary to manipulate the rheostat for hand pieces or other dental equipment. The body must be able to work from a dental stool in order to perform most dental procedures. The ability to sit and stand for an extended period of time is also necessary. Other specific requirements include color spectrum differentiation; manual dexterity/motor coordination, hand-eye coordination, physical communications; visual acuity and communication/language development. Individuals in this position may be exposed to the following: bloodborne pathogens; chemical hazards (skin irritants); nitrous oxide; vibrating equipment; use of sharp instruments; and latex. Education and Experience Qualifications: Required: 3 months experience (3 courses) in dental office practices and procedures; 3 months experience (3 courses) in dental operatory practices and procedures; 3 months experience (3 courses) in four-handed assisting techniques; 3 months experience (3 courses) in inventory record-keeping; 3 months experience (300 hrs. training) in care of dental equipment; 1 month experience (100 hrs. training) in using a computer. Current CPR/BLS certification and radiographer license required at all times throughout employment and chair side dental assistant experience required. Basic computer literacy including familiarity with Microsoft Office and internet/email is required to perform clerical responsibilities. Commercial Drivers License (CDL) required within 6 months from hire. Desired: Experience and knowledge of a wide variety of dental instruments and procedures, especially those involving pediatric dentistry procedures; experience in an educational and/or hospital setting, experience with electronic health record is desired. Additional Information: Location: Postle Hall (0024) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-Hospital/Occupational-Therapist_R146207-2": {
      "title": "Occupational Therapist (OT) Acute Inpatient",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Occupational Therapist (OT) Acute Inpatient Department: University Hospital | Rehabilitation Services, Acute Care Rehabilitation team members are licensed or certified professionals (physical therapists, occupational therapists, speech/language pathologists, social workers or therapeutic recreation specialists who work within a specific team structure to offer inpatient or outpatient rehabilitation services.  These services are offered to the acute-care hospital, the acute inpatient rehabilitation facility (Dodd Hall), or outpatient service sites to patients who have disorders and conditions associated primarily with traumatic brain injury, spinal cord injury, stroke, or other neurogenic disorders, orthopedic problems, burns, amputations, or chronic pain.  The rehabilitation team members report to the rehabilitation team leaders as part of the overall Rehabilitation Services division structure.    The therapy staff still reports to the rehabilitation team manager for all supervisory tasks. Each rehabilitation team member is first a part of a group effort to provide care within a continuous performance improvement environment, and secondly a distinct professional who provides specific contributions to the team approach.  Team members assess patients and establish together plans of care; provide a wide variety of treatment techniques; provide education and support to families; and facilitate continuing care planning. Team members evaluate quality of services and participate in outcomes management activities.  Although team members report directly to a team leader, they are also responsible to each other, to those they supervise (rehab assistants and aides) and to other participants in patient care activities, including attending and resident physicians, nurses, their support staff, and Patient Care Resource Managers, to assure coordination of services and programs.  A team member embraces the Intensive Caring values of the organization and uses them to guide interactions with others. The occupational therapist (OT) will also provide specialized treatments to help the patient explore and identify productive avocational interests.  Treatments include assessment of interests, introduction to various methods used to explore resources post discharge (use of the internet, identification of local organizations, methods to inquire about resources), exposure to local organizations, and education material to maximize patient post discharge planning.  The OT is expected to be the contact for the community link and be a liaison for patients/staff/consumers of Rehabilitation Services. Minimum Education Bachelor's Degree in Occupational Therapy and Licensed as a Occupational Therapist in State of Ohio. Additional Information: \"Acute Care Occupational Therapists are licensed professional responsible for evaluating, planning, and implementing occupational therapy services for hospitalized patients with acute medical, surgical, neurological, orthopedic, cardiopulmonary, and traumatic conditions. Working as part of an interdisciplinary healthcare team, the Occupational Therapist promotes safe participation in activities of daily living (ADLs), functional mobility, cognition, upper extremity function, discharge planning, and patient/family education to maximize independence and support a safe transition to the next level of care. Occupational Therapists provide services throughout the acute care hospital, collaborating closely with physicians, nursing staff, rehabilitation professionals, case management, and other healthcare providers. The Occupational Therapist reports to the Rehabilitation Manager within the Rehabilitation Services organizational structure for all supervisory and performance-related responsibilities.\" Location: University Hospital (0870) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ross-Heart-Hospital/Occupational-Therapist_R145709-2": {
      "title": "Occupational Therapist (OT) - Acute Inpatient",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Occupational Therapist (OT) - Acute Inpatient Department: Ross | Inpatient Rehab Rehabilitation team members are licensed or certified professionals (physical therapists, occupational therapists, speech/language pathologists, social workers or therapeutic recreation specialists who work within a specific team structure to offer inpatient or outpatient rehabilitation services.  These services are offered to the acute-care hospital, the acute inpatient rehabilitation facility (Dodd Hall), or outpatient service sites to patients who have disorders and conditions associated primarily with traumatic brain injury, spinal cord injury, stroke, or other neurogenic disorders, orthopedic problems, burns, amputations, or chronic pain.  The rehabilitation team members report to the rehabilitation team leaders as part of the overall Rehabilitation Services division structure.  Dodd Hall utilizes a matrix management system where each diagnostic team has a team leader who oversees the team programming.  The therapy staff still reports to the rehabilitation team leader for all supervisory tasks. Each rehabilitation team member is first a part of a group effort to provide care within a continuous performance improvement environment, and secondly a distinct professional who provides specific contributions to the team approach.  Team members assess patients and establish together plans of care; provide a wide variety of treatment techniques; provide education and support to families; and facilitate continuing care planning. Team members evaluate  quality of services and participate in outcomes management activities.  Although team members report directly to a team leader, they are also responsible to each other, to those they supervise (rehab assistants and aides) and to other participants in patient care activities, including attending and resident physicians, nurses, their support staff, and Patient Care Resource Managers, to assure coordination of services and programs.  A team member embraces the Intensive Caring values of the organization and uses them to guide interactions with others. The occupational therapist (OT) will also provide specialized treatments to help the patient explore and identify productive avocational interests.  Treatments include assessment of interests, introduction to various methods used to explore resources post discharge (use of the internet, identification of local organizations, methods to inquire about resources), exposure to local organizations, and educational material to maximize patient post discharge planning.   The OT is expected to be the contact for the community link and be a liaison for patients/staff/consumers of Rehabilitation Services. Minimum Qualifications All rehabilitation team members must be licensed and/or certified with the respective profession Occupational therapy, and meet the educational and/or certification requirements established by their profession. Occupational therapists must hold bachelor’s degrees.  All academic degrees must have been granted by an accredited institution.  An Occupational Therapist must hold a conditional license in the state of Ohio.  All licensed professionals must be cleared through the National Database of Practitioners.  Typically, one-two years of experience working in a medical setting is preferred for all professionals hired. Additional Information: Location: Ross Heart Hospital (0353) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
