    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-Hospital/Staff-Nurse--RN----Acute-Care---General-Medicine_R151074-1": {
      "title": "Staff Nurse (RN) - Acute Care - General Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Staff Nurse (RN) - Acute Care - General Medicine Department: University Hospital | 11 West Doan Hall General Medicine Job Description Scope of Position: The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center?s mission is to improve health in Ohio and across the world through innovation in research, education, and patient care. The team provides patient care and supportive services directed towards achievement of positive patient care outcomes, maximizing the patient?s involvement in his/her own plan of care and reducing the length of hospitalization, The staff nurse plays a critical role in staff engagement , the patient experience, quality and safety, and cost effective care. Position Summary: The Staff Nurse is responsible for managing and providing care to the patient and his/her family, and for directing and supervising nursing care provided by other members of the patient care team. The Staff Nurse is responsible for assessing, planning, implementing, coordinating, delegating and evaluating the nursing care of patients in alignment with the professional practice model. Minimum Education Required Bachelor's Level Degree or equivalent combination of education and experience Required Qualifications Degree in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program required. Current Ohio license or interim permit. *Experience in relevant care setting preferred. Additional Information: 11 West Doan is 27-bed unit in the Acute Care Department. We care for a wide variety of patients. However, we specialize in patients with medical issues that range from acutely ill to long term illness and disease management. On our unit, nurses work directly with attending physicians to deliver optimal care in a team-centered environment. 11 West Doan is a wonderful place to learn and grow. Our nursing practice is staff-driven through our Unit Leadership Committee and Evidence-Bas. Our team is passionate about staff development and advancement. 11 West Doan will be moving to our new inpatient tower very soon! Location: University Hospital - Doan Hall (0089) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 36 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Visual-Media-Producer_R157626-1": {
      "title": "Visual Media Producer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Visual Media Producer Department: Athletics | Digital Media Job Description Responsible for all aspects of operation and preparation for the department video boards; including athletics events and non-athletics events. Must be able to quickly acquire, edit and package footage for creation of in-game and post game video features. Consults with the Big Ten Network and establishes a video highlight share and ease of distribution for rights agreement. Assists network television with feed and footage/highlight needs. Schedules and assigns coverage for each team's video filming. Produces video for highlight films, banquets, the website and other needs. Films practices, competitions, press conferences and other events. Hires, trains and supervises student assistants. Establishes staffing needs and schedules for video board and event coverage. Performs other duties as assigned. Position requires working evenings and weekends. Position may require the completion of a criminal background check.   Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. 2 years of relevant experience required. 2-4 years of relevant experience preferred. Considerable experience in video production services, preferably in a sports environment. Experience and knowledge of field and studio production techniques. Knowledge of post production techniques including inter-format, non-linear and high-end digital editing as well as digital composition. Knowledge and experience with video graphics software including Adobe Photo Shop, Premier, Avid and After Effects. FUNCTION: Marketing and Communications SUB-FUNCTION: Videography CAREER BAND: Specialized CAREER LEVEL: S2 Additional Information: Location: Fawcett Center for Tomorrow (0284) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Wooster-Campus/Greenhouse-Student-Assistant---ATI_R158049": {
      "title": "Greenhouse Student Assistant - ATI",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Greenhouse Student Assistant - ATI Department: FAES | ATI Plant Science Engineering Technologies-JM The Weekend Greenhouse Waterer is responsible for monitoring and maintaining greenhouse crops during weekends and university breaks to ensure plant health and quality. This position requires an individual who is dependable, observant, and capable of working independently while following established greenhouse protocols. The employee will assist with watering, environmental monitoring, facility upkeep, and basic crop maintenance in the OSU Wooster Campus greenhouses. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Water greenhouse crops according. Monitor plant health and report signs of water stress, nutrient deficiencies, pests, diseases, or other crop concerns. Check greenhouse environmental conditions, including temperature, humidity, and irrigation system performance. Apply fertilizers as directed and assist with preparing fertilizer solutions when needed. Perform general greenhouse maintenance, including: Sweeping greenhouse floors and hallways Cleaning work areas Washing pots and trays Emptying trash and debris Assist with planting, transplanting, and basic crop care as needed. Help maintain a clean, safe, and organized work environment. Follow integrated pest management (IPM) practices and report pest or disease issues. Complete assigned tasks independently while communicating concerns to greenhouse staff. Qualifications Previous greenhouse, horticulture, agriculture, or plant-care experience preferred. Basic knowledge of plant watering and care practices preferred. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision. Strong attention to detail and ability to follow instructions. Reliable, responsible, and punctual. Basic computer skills are helpful but not required. Excellent communication and organizational skills. Must have reliable mode of transportation. Physical Requirements Ability to stand, walk, bend, lift, and carry items throughout the work shift. Ability to lift to 30 pounds. Ability to work in varying greenhouse environmental conditions, including heat and humidity. Ability to safely operate watering equipment and basic greenhouse tools. Working Conditions Work is performed primarily in greenhouse facilities on the OSU Wooster Campus. Duties may involve exposure to varying temperatures, humidity levels, soil, fertilizers, and greenhouse production materials. Professional Expectations Demonstrate professionalism and dependability. Exercise good judgment and take ownership of assigned responsibilities. Provide excellent customer service to faculty, staff, students, and visitors. Represent The Ohio State University, ATI, and CFAES with integrity and professionalism while supporting the university's mission and shared values. Schedule Weekend shifts during the academic year, summer, holiday periods, and university breaks as assigned. Typical responsibilities include checking greenhouse crops, watering, monitoring environmental conditions, and maintaining facility cleanliness during non-business hours. Additional Information: Location: Skou Hall (0643) Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 10 Shift: Weekend Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Wooster-Campus/Student-Research-Assistant-2---HCS_R158004-2": {
      "title": "Student Research Assistant 2 - HCS",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Student Research Assistant 2 - HCS Department: FAES | Horticulture and Crop Science-JM The Vegetable Production Systems Laboratory in the Department of Horticulture and Crop Science located on The OSU-Wooster Campus ( https://proxy.qualtrics.com/proxy/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fu.osu.edu%2Fvegprolab%2F&token=lDe1D7S76H0PhqCO2XJnyO8uKdYc%2F%2FMx3XEB%2BRHy03E%3D ) invites you or someone you recommend to contact us about positions available with our team. Many skills are required to complete our work and we are currently recruiting new team members for part and full-time positions. These positions are ideal for people looking to align their workday with their interests and abilities. What is important to know about this opportunity, our team, and what we do and why includes the following: We address real-world challenges and opportunities faced by vegetable growers managing small to large farms across Ohio, the region, and globe. Our research and educational resources impact many people. We study vegetables, and vegetable farming as it is and could be done. We focus on tools and practices expected to improve the success and resilience of vegetable farms and quality of food they produce. We work year-round ... outside, in high tunnels and greenhouses, and in laboratories and offices. Individual tasks completed in all these settings vary, so they accommodate team members with different interests and abilities. Also, our activities change over time. This creates opportunities to learn and do different things. Experience with these topics or in these settings is not required. Bring your willingness to learn and put in solid effort and you will succeed. Knowledge and abilities you develop are useful in other areas of work. We do NOT study pesticides, herbicides, insecticides, fungicides, or similar materials. We do occasionally study fertilizers and other materials applied to plants and soils. We combine critical thinking with thoughtful action to meet our objectives. We are constantly learning -- applying trusted methods but always looking to improve them and address new challenges and opportunities. We are serious about what we do and enjoy it. We offer schedule flexibility. Positions are located on The Ohio State University Wooster Campus. Additional Job Description Please contact me to learn more. Dr. Matt Kleinhenz Professor, Extension Specialist (Vegetable Production Systems) kleinhenz.1@osu.edu Additional Information: Location: Gourley Hall (0405) Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 10 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Undergrad-Research-Assistant-2_R157639-2": {
      "title": "Undergrad Research Assistant 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Undergrad Research Assistant 2 Department: FAES | Animal Sciences-JM The Undergraduate Research Assistant will assist with ongoing meat science and muscle biology research through sample collection and preparation, laboratory analyses, data collection and entry, and general laboratory maintenance. The student will gain hands-on experience in meat science research, laboratory techniques, data management, and scientific research while working closely with graduate students, staff, and faculty. Responsibilities will require attention to detail, reliability, adherence to laboratory safety protocols, and the ability to work both independently and as part of a research team. Additional Information: Location: Animal Science Building (0156) Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 10 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-Hospital/Clinic-Nurse--RN----Chemotherapy_R156853-1": {
      "title": "Clinic Nurse (RN) - Chemotherapy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Clinic Nurse (RN) - Chemotherapy Department: James | James 300 Chemotherapy Scope of Position The Ohio State University Comprehensive Cancer Center - James Cancer Hospital and Solove Research Institute’s (OSUCCC-James) mission is to improve health in Ohio and across the world through innovation in research, education, and patient care. The team provides patient care and supportive services directed towards achievement of positive patient care outcomes, maximizing the patient’s involvement in their own plan of care, and reducing the length of hospitalization, the clinic nurse plays a critical role in staff engagement, the patient experience, quality and safety, and cost-effective care. Position Summary The Clinic Nurse is responsible for managing and providing care to the patient and their family, and for directing and supervising nursing care provided by other members of the patient care team. The Clinic Nurse is responsible for assessing, planning, implementing, coordinating, delegating, and evaluating the nursing care of patients in alignment with the professional practice model. Required Qualifications Degree in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program required. Current Ohio license or interim permit. *Experience in relevant care setting preferred. Additional Information: The unit provides specialized inpatient oncology care for patients undergoing chemotherapy and treatment for complex cancer diagnoses. As part of The Ohio State University Comprehensive Cancer Center – James Cancer Hospital and Solove Research Institute, the unit delivers evidence-based, multidisciplinary care focused on patient safety, treatment excellence, and compassionate support. Nurses and healthcare professionals collaborate closely with oncology physicians, advanced practice providers, pharmacists, and support services to manage chemotherapy administration, symptom management, and specialized cancer care while advancing the organization's mission of improving lives through innovation in research, education, and patient care. Hours 730a-6p Location: University Hospital - Pavilion (0372) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Health-System-Shared-Services/Nursing-Professional-Practice---Governance-Specialist_R157273": {
      "title": "Nursing Professional Practice & Governance Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Nursing Professional Practice & Governance Specialist Department: Health System Shared Services | HS Nursing Enterprise Leadership Scope of Position The Ohio State University Medical Wexner Medical Center (OSUWMC) mission is focused on integrating quality patient care, education. and research. In conjunction with the Director of Enterprise Nursing Quality, Patient Safety, and Evidence-Based Practice (EBP), the Staff Associate role leads medical center wide efforts across all inpatient and outpatient settings in establishing a culture of evidence-based professional nursing practice. The Program Director provides leadership and direction to all levels of nurses regarding the design, implementation and evaluation of evidence-based professional nursing standards of practice and EBP initiatives. Position Summary The Staff Associate oversees and provides direction for the assessment, planning, implementation and evaluation of evidence-based nursing projects for the enterprise and leads and oversees the review and creation of all nursing policies and procedures for the Medical Center. In partnership with internal and external customers, the Staff Associate works with individuals in a way that ensures that evidence-based practice is understandable and measurable. He/she works to ensure a shared sense of purpose in creating both value for the customer and the committed involvement of nursing staff at all levels. The Staff Associate serves as a leader and mentor both in the department and throughout OSUWMC. The Staff Associate demonstrates an analytical and intellectual understanding of best practices and their impact on quality of patient care. Staff Associate-level responsibilities include: maintain a professional presence throughout the enterprise , oversee and maintain evidence -based standards of practice, collaborating and integrating services within the department (nursing  quality and nursing research) and with other departments; assist in maintaining a collaborative partnership with The Ohio State University College of Nursing and Academic Practice Partnership work with nursing services to ensure the delivery of evidence-based practice across all levels of nursing personnel across the medical center; assess and improve evidence-based resources and service. across the enterprise.   Minimum Qualifications Masters Degree in Nursing, Healthcare Administration, or Business Administration required. Doctoral degree preferred (PhD, DNP).  8 years of relevant experience required. 12 or more years of relevant experience preferred. Licensed to practice as a registered nurse in the State of Ohio. Experience in leading evidence-based practice change initiatives on a microsystem & macrosystem level. Skilled in program planning, project management, and leading nursing and interdisciplinary teams; previous experience in an academic medical center and/or a health system preferred. Additional Information: This position has a good mix of policy/program oversight while also working to expand evidence-based practice throughout the organization. Additionally, they have a significant connection to the College of Nursing through the OSU College of Nursing & Academic Practice Partnership and the OSUWMC/DNP/DNE Student Project Approval Committee. The ideal candidate would have the ability to be detail-oriented and oversee the nursing policy as well as form good relationships with the College of Nursing and partners across the organization to expand EBP. 40 hour a week position, Monday-Friday. Location: Ackerman Rd, 600 (2435) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/OSU-Health-Plan/Switchboard-Operator---2nd-Shift_R156501-1": {
      "title": "Switchboard Operator - 2nd Shift",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Switchboard Operator - 2nd Shift Department: Health System Shared Services | Switchboard Scope of Position Serves as the primary contact person for all of OSUMC healthcare network which functions as a centralized information hub within the medical center. This position answers, routes and triages critical and non-critical calls 365 days a year, 24 hours a day. This position involves screening for patient information; digital paging; public address announcements; answers, communicates and documents emergent calls; handles after-hours answering service calls; maintains database and on-call schedules; provides technical support for or pager issues; supports assigned weekend on-call rotations & trains new staff (other duties as assigned) Position Summary Responsible for superior front-line customer service while processing internal and external communications through an integrated computer telephony system. This role involves multi-tasking within several computer applications and the ability to think critically in a fast-paced 24/7 business environment. The ability to quickly gather critical information and electronically communicate to the correct team is vital to this role. The capability to learn quickly and readily adapt to ongoing change to technology and process is essential for success in this role. Our switchboard operators play a critical role in the success of the medical center operations and take pride in caring for our patients & customers Minimum Qualifications Must be available to work 3 pm to 11:30 pm, every other weekend. High School diploma or GED. Certification or vocational training may be preferred. 1 year of relevant experience required. 2-4 years of relevant experience preferred. Our Comprehensive Employee Benefits Include An array of retirement plan options, each with a generous employer contribution. Affordable health insurance options, including dental, vision and prescription coverage that begin on day one. Paid vacation and sick leave, including short and long-term disability and paid parental leave. Get the most out of the Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. And much more!  Additional Information: Location: Ackerman Rd, 700 (0921) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/College-of-MedicineOffice-of-Health-Sciences/PhD-Faculty---Radiology--Translational-Biomedical-Imaging-Research_R127243-1": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor - Faculty - Radiology, Translational Biomedical Imaging Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. You will be presented with the opportunity to attach up to five (5) documents in the Application Documents section. If necessary, please consider combining documents into one file. If you require any assistance with including the necessary documents in the application process, please reach out to HRConnection@osu.edu . Resume parsing is not effective on documents which exceed one (1) page.  As a result, it is not recommended to select Autofill with Resume when applying if using a resume or CV which exceeds one (1) page. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Associate/Full Professor - Faculty - Radiology, Translational Biomedical Imaging Research Department: Medicine | Radiology Tenure faculty (regardless of rank) - persons with the titles of professor, associate professor, assistant professor and instructor who serve on appointments totaling 50% or more service to the university and who are eligible for tenure or who have obtained tenure. Duties and responsibilities are assigned in accordance with the workload guidelines laid out in the pattern of administration of each faculty member’s tenure initiation unit (TIU) and, as appropriate, regional campus; obligations will include research, service and/or teaching or clinical practice.  These faculty will have earned doctorate or other terminal degree in the relevant field of study or possession of equivalent experience. Additional Information: Faculty – Radiology, Translational Biomedical Imaging Research The Ohio State University College of Medicine and the Wexner Medical Center are seeking faculty in translational biomedical imaging research. This position is available at the Associate Professor or Full Professor level. Senior faculty appointments require a minimum of 50% salary support from external funding sources. Position Overview The Department of Radiology at The Ohio State University (OSU) is seeking experienced candidates for tenure-track faculty positions in translational biomedical imaging research at the rank of associate or full professor. Rank and startup package are commensurate with academic record and experience. The OSU College of Medicine and Department of Radiology have made significant commitments towards expanding medical imaging research and are seeking outstanding candidates in the field of neuroimaging who are dedicated to advancing translational research and innovation, committed to education, and inspire inclusive excellence. He/she/they will contribute to the Department’s ambition while upholding the organization’s mission and values.  We are specifically seeking candidates with interest in translational research in MRI and/or molecular imaging applications in neuroscience. Department/Division Overview The Department of Radiology is rapidly growing, with expanded services at off-site imaging centers, and renovations to our existing clinical spaces and new spaces through the medical center strategic expansion project ($3+ Billion):   Main campus: New construction of a state-of-the-art 830-bed hospital tower, a biomedical research tower, and a Health Sciences building that will house the College of Medicine  Around the city: Construction of 2 newly designed ambulatory care centers in New Albany and Dublin  now completed and open in addition to 16 established ambulatory care centers up and running today The benefits of working for The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center: Competitive base salary with ample additional income opportunities  Unmatched Retirement Benefits: 14% employer match Eligible to participate in 403(b) and 457(b) Supplemental Retirement Accounts Increased retirement savings through Retirement Continuation Plan 415(m) Exceptional health, vision, and dental benefits, including: Health Reimbursement Account  Healthcare Flexible Spending Account Dependent Care Flexible Spending Account  Family Building Assistance and Benefits Lifestyle Spending Accounts Childcare Programs Eligible for Public Service Loan Forgiveness and institutional support to fulfill requirements  Tuition Assistance Plan covers, up to: 10 credit hours per term for faculty and staff 50% of a dependent’s fees per semester 11 Recognized Annual Holidays Annual Leave Accruals: 15 days of Sick Time 22 days of Vacation Time Generous CME allowance As part of the College of Medicine at the Ohio State Wexner Medical Center (OSUWMC, Academics & Research | Ohio State Medical Center (osu.edu)), the Department of Radiology (Radiology Department I Ohio State College of Medicine (osu.edu)) provides an academic home for medical imaging research and training at Ohio State. Faculty in the College of Medicine have access to resources to assist in grant writing, management, and to stimulate collaboration, and has established resources in clinical data and high-performance computing and data storage. The Ohio State University is one of the nation’s largest integrated health sciences campuses, with access to a CTSA-funded Center for Clinical and Translational Science and a state-of-the-art 1 million square foot, NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center. The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center and James Comprehensive Cancer Center are nationally recognized for clinical, educational, and research excellence. We are one of the largest health systems in the state of Ohio. The Ohio State University College of Medicine has annual research funding of over $400M, including NIH grant funding of $237M. The Department of Radiology has over 70 faculty members and a large array of imaging facilities on the main OSU campus and at multiple satellite clinics across central Ohio, conducive to clinical research. The Wright Center of Innovation in Biomedical Imaging houses imaging research faculty and an array of imaging equipment, including Siemens 0.55T Free.Max, 3T Vida, and Philips 3T MRI systems, plus a Philips Vereos PET/CT scanner. The newly opened Carmenton Innovation District includes the Pelotonia Research Center and James Outpatient Care Center that houses Ohio’s first proton therapy center. Construction is also underway on a state-of-the-art 830-bed hospital tower, a biomedical research tower, and a Health Sciences building that will house the College of Medicine.  By joining our faculty, you will have excellent opportunities for advancement, while working with an exceptional cadre of multidisciplinary providers.  Faculty are supported by many outstanding clinical, research, and educational resources in the department and institution, including substantial, dedicated expertise in imaging technology innovation, artificial intelligence, and health services research. Duties and Responsibilities Successful candidates are expected to develop and lead an independent research program and participate in institutional efforts to translate novel imaging technologies and methodologies into clinical practice. They are expected to secure grant funding, mentor trainees, and work collaboratively with investigators across the College of Medicine and the university.  Requirements Senior level appointment requires an established history of research accomplishment and grant funding, as well as active grants. Successful applicants should hold a Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering, Medical Physics, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Bioinformatics, or a related discipline, with scientific collaboration and research interests in the following areas: · Translational research in MRI and/or molecular imaging applications in neuroscience. Any questions can be directed to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Orlando Simonetti (orlando.simonetti@osumc.edu). Evaluation of applications is underway and will continue until positions are filled. How to Apply To be considered, application materials must include a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a statement of research plans (limited to 3 pages), and a statement of teaching and mentoring. All inquiries and nominations should be directed in confidence to: Anna Godwin, Research Faculty Recruiter at Anna.Godwin@osumc.edu. Faculty Defined Clinical faculty (regardless of rank) - Persons with titles of assistant professor-clinical, associate professor-clinical and professor-clinical. These faculty will have earned a doctor of medicine (MD), doctorate (PhD) or other terminal degree in the relevant field. Clinical faculty members are not eligible for tenure and are appointed for terms of three to five years. They may be reappointed to successive terms. Their principal career focus is the delivery of exemplary clinical care, and may include teaching, and/or research.  Tenure-Track faculty (regardless of rank) - Persons with the titles of assistant professor, associate professor, or professor who are eligible for tenure or who have obtained tenure. These faculty will have earned a doctorate (PhD), Doctor of Medicine (MD) or other terminal degree in the relevant field of study. Their primary career focus centers on research, service, and teaching. Tenure-track faculty with MD or MD/PhD degrees may also be involved in clinical care. Research Faculty (regardless of rank) - Persons with the titles of research assistant professor, research associate professor, or research professor. These faculty will have earned a doctorate (PhD) or other terminal degree in the relevant field of study. Research faculty members are not eligible for tenure and are appointed for terms of one to five years. Their principal career focus is research. The Ohio State University College of Medicine  The Ohio State University College of Medicine, with more than 5,000 learners, is the only academic medical center in central Ohio. Ranked as the 28th Best Medical School – Research, 40th Best Medical School – Primary Care, it is known nationwide for curricular innovation, pioneering research, and outstanding patient care at The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center. With more than 2,600 faculty members, the college comprises 20 clinical departments, eight basic science departments and a School of Health and Rehabilitation Sciences. The Wexner Medical Center The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center consists of The Ohio State University Health System, the College of Medicine, the Health Sciences Library and the Faculty Group Practice. The Ohio State Wexner Medical Center is committed to providing world-class care. At the Ohio State Wexner Medical Center, we're proud to be celebrating our 31st consecutive year ranked in the U.S. News & World Report Best Hospitals list. This year, the Ohio State Wexner Medical Center has 10 nationally ranked specialties out of 15 and two selected as high performing. U.S. News & World Report consistently ranks the Ohio State Wexner Medical Center as the top hospital in Columbus. The Wexner Medical Center is rated as high performing in 14 out of 20 common procedures and conditions, including abdominal aortic aneurysm repair, aortic valve surgery, heart attack, heart bypass surgery and heart failure. The University  Eligible Ohio State employees receive comprehensive benefits packages, including medical, dental and vision insurance, tuition assistance for employees and their dependents, and state or alternative retirement options with competitive employer contributions. Ohio State is a dynamic community where opportunity thrives, and individuals transform themselves and their world. Positions are available in countless fields and specialties. Become a Buckeye and contribute to an incredible legacy that serves to guide our future and shape a better tomorrow. The Ohio State University is committed to enhancing academic excellence. Recruiting, supporting, and retaining faculty of the highest caliber is a core component of this commitment. The Office of Academic Affairs (OAA) has established Dual Careers and Faculty Relocation (DCFR) to focus on supporting new and prospective faculty and their loved ones. Service offerings include dual careers partner consultations, identifying potential employers and/or employment opportunities, consultation and resources related to relocation, as well as identifying opportunities to engage on campus and in the surrounding community. While employment opportunities are not guaranteed, resources and consultation are provided to support the partners of new and prospective faculty as they are considering or transitioning to The Ohio State University.  In addition to being responsive to dual-career opportunities, we strongly promote work-life balance to support our community members through a suite of institutionalized policies.  Ohio State is an NSF ADVANCE institution and a member of the Ohio/Western Pennsylvania/West Virginia Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC).  Columbus, Ohio The area offers a wide range of affordable housing, many cultural and recreational opportunities, excellent schools, and a strong economy based on government as well as service, transportation, and technology industries. Additional information about the Columbus area is available here. In addition to  its Columbus campus, Ohio State has four regional campuses including Ohio State Lima, Ohio State Mansfield, Ohio State Marion, and Ohio State Newark, in addition to Ohio State ATI in Wooster.   The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability. Location: Twelfth Ave, 395 W (0356) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift The Ohio State University believes in diversity in people and ideas. What Ohio State does matters. And how we do it matters. When we are at our best, we make a real difference to people. Our size, breadth, geography, history and standard of excellence position us to drive the future of higher education. We believe that the university should be a place where people can work and learn together in a safe environment, free of violence, harassment, discrimination, exploitation, or intimidation. As such, finalists for any faculty position that carries tenure must sign an authorization and disclosure form, which will allow current or prior employer(s) to share information to the University regarding any findings of employment-related misconduct or disciplinary proceedings against a candidate and/or any pending investigations related to alleged misconduct. Such information shall include findings and pending investigations with respect to sexual harassment, violence, or harassment; research misconduct; financial fraud or misconduct; foreign influence violations, grant misuse or misconduct; and/or any other type of finding or pending investigation relating to a candidate’s employer’s policies and rules governing faculty conduct that may reasonably be expected to affect a candidate’s appointment. If the University becomes aware of any past finding of misconduct or pending investigations that were not disclosed, Ohio State will treat that as a serious omission and reserves the right to rescind an offer or terminate employment. Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Senior-Engineer---Additive-Manufacturing_R151155-1": {
      "title": "Senior Engineer – Additive Manufacturing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Senior Engineer – Additive Manufacturing Department: Engineering | Center for Design and Manufacturing Excellence The Senior Engineer develops, executes, and leads additive manufacturing research and development efforts for the Center for Design and Manufacturing Excellence (CDME); works closely and interacts with industry partners to scope out projects and statements of work; manages and executes entire sales process with customers and associated support staff; serves as lead writer on technical reports and proposals to sponsoring agencies; works closely with OSU faculty, CDME staff and students to coordinate multi-disciplinary engineering tasks; executes technical engineering work through use of personal expertise, advanced manufacturing equipment, and software; ensures projects are completed in accordance with project milestones, deliverable requirements and within the agreed upon cost and schedule; partners with division director to ensure disciplined internal project management processes are followed; utilizes advanced technical expertise and established leadership skills in determining the most direct path for successful project execution; contributes to business development activities by researching funding opportunities, traveling to customer facilities for project meetings, and presenting research results at conferences and symposia; establishes priorities and supervises student employees (e.g. provides developmental opportunities, coaches to foster development, evaluates performance); supports professional development and student program activities of CDME in area of expertise; responsible for bringing in sufficient funding to support position and any direct reports; performs special projects and other duties as assigned. This position will require access to export controlled data and work in an export controlled facility. Eligibility for this position is restricted to “U.S. persons” as defined in U.S. export control regulations. “U.S. persons” include: (1) U.S. citizens or nationals; (2) permanent residents; (3) asylees or refugees; or (4) individuals otherwise described as “protected individuals” pursuant to Title 8 U.S. Code Section 1324b(a)(3)(b). Additional Information: Qualifications: Education Required: Bachelor's Degree: Major: Mechanical Engineering, Materials Science, Electrical Engineering, Applied Physics Desired: Master's Degree: Major: Mechanical Engineering, Materials Science, Electrical Engineering, Applied Physics Experience Required: At least 4 years working in additive manufacturing, running equipment and developing technology for laser powder bed fusion machines. Experience developing new materials, running in situ sensing systems, and calibrating laser systems. CAD experience designing parts or mechanical systems. Demonstrable experience in project management and proposal writing, with at least 1 proposal awarded. Extensive experience in a professional multi-disciplinary research environment with experience in customer engagement; considerable experience in a R & D setting (i.e., planning and conducting R & D projects/programs in terms of technical and managerial functions) Desired: Experience developing novel additive manufacturing processes or approaches, including advanced laser technology utilization or multimaterial processes. Experience with electrical systems in additive manufacturing equipment. Experience working with students. The target hiring range for this job profile is $88,300 - $115,350 . The actual salary paid to an individual will vary based on multiple factors, including but not limit to, education, years of experience, internal equity, etc. Location: Research Center (0073) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/HR-Service-Center-Representative-2_R156393-1": {
      "title": "HR Service Center Representative 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: HR Service Center Representative 2 Department: Human Resources | Core Services Shared Services Your Next Chapter: Welcome to a fast-paced, people-centered environment where every day brings something new. As part of our HR Service Center team, you will be at the heart of employee support—fielding a high volume of inbound calls, written inquiries, and in-person interactions from a broad audience that includes faculty, staff, student employees, retirees, and prospective hires. Whether it is a quick question or a complex situation, you’ll be the first line of guidance, empathy, and resolution. This is a hybrid role, combining remote work with on-site responsibilities in a fast-paced call center environment. Our team operates Monday through Friday from 8:00 AM and 5:00 PM – offering a stable schedule that supports a healthy work-life balance. You’ll collaborate closely with a tight-knit group of professionals who support each other, share knowledge, and celebrate wins—big and small. We’re looking for curious problem-solvers who thrive on learning and love helping others. If you're a self-starter who can stay calm in unpredictable situations, handle sensitive conversations with grace, and bring a friendly, professional demeanor to every interaction, you’ll fit right in. This role is perfect for someone who enjoys variety, values teamwork, and wants to make a real impact through meaningful human connection. Your Day-to-Day Serves as the primary contact for incoming HR and payroll-related inquiries via phone, email, mail, in-person and Self Service. Provides timely and accurate support to a wide range of individuals—including current and former employees, retirees, their dependents, and external partners. Resolves issues of low to moderate complexity independently and escalates more complex matters to the appropriate Service Center resources, ensuring consistent and precise handling of every inquiry. Provide guidance on university policies, benefits, payroll, and employment procedures. Maintain confidentiality while handling sensitive employee information. Assist with onboarding and offboarding processes. Partner with HR Shared Services teams to navigate and resolve complex inquiries, ensuring seamless coordination and accurate resolution across HR functions. Support HR initiatives and contribute to process improvements. The Ideal Candidate Will Have: High school diploma or equivalent Minimum 1 year of experience in human resources, customer service, and/or inbound call center. Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize effectively. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, Workday, and case system platforms Bonus Points If You Have: Advanced training or education in a related field. Background in shared services, call center, higher education, or related industries such as insurance. Familiarity with Workday or similar HR systems. Additional Information: To Apply: Please submit your resume and a cover letter as part of your application. In your cover letter, we’d love to hear about: Your relevant experience – Describe previous customer service roles (e.g., retail, call center, administrative support). The soft skills that make you a great fit. Any transferable skills or experiences that you believe would add value to this role. We are excited to learn more about you and how you see yourself contributing to our team! Interested in knowing more about HR at OSU? Check out our website by clicking here . Salary Range: $18.37-$23.99* Function: Human Resources Sub-function: HR Service Center Career Band: Individual Contributor – Technical Career Level: T2 Working at Ohio State comes with a great mix of rewards and benefits. From competitive pay and top-notch health coverage to retirement plans, tuition help, and leadership training—we have got you covered. You will also enjoy access to on-site childcare, campus sports, arts events, and more. Check out all the details at hr.osu.edu/benefits . *The offer for this position will fall within this range based on internal equity, the unit’s available budget, and the candidate’s qualifications. Location: Gateway C (0863) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-Hospital/Lactation-Consultant_R156825-1": {
      "title": "Lactation Consultant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Lactation Consultant Department: University Hospital | Women and Infants Administration Scope of Position   The Lactation Consultant (LC) collaborates with the patient care team, other health care professionals and the community to provide patients with breast feeding knowledge and skill. The lactation consultant is responsible for the overall planning, direction, and evaluation of breast-feeding education for the Department of women and Infants Nursing and the Medical Center. The focus of care is breast feeding education for patients, the community, and health care providers. The Department of Women and Infants Nursing provides comprehensive breastfeeding education to inpatients, outpatients, and the community on a 24-hr basis. Position Summary   Responsible for assessing, planning, managing, coordinating, directing, and evaluating breast feeding education provided to patients and their family/ support persons by the patient care team in Department of Women’s and Infants Nursing. The LC prioritizes breast feeding education needs of patients and collaborates with the patient care team and other health care providers. Ongoing community education and agency collaboration is essential. Minimum Qualifications      For Hire: Graduate of an accredited school of Registered Nursing. Baccalaureate degree in nursing or related field desired; current Ohio license, certification as a lactation consultant preferred; previous nursing experience in a relevant healthcare setting preferred; prior patient education and women and infant nursing experience desired.    Ongoing: Maintain Ohio RN license; meet mandatory educational and health requirements; maintain knowledge related to patient care issues, quality improvement and cost reduction, current policies, procedures, and protocols. Attain IBCLC within one year of hire if not already certified. Additional Information: Hours could be 11a-11p or 1a -1p The Lactation Consultant is a key member of the Women’s and Infant Services team at The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center. This role provides expert lactation support, education, and counseling to mothers and families, promoting successful breastfeeding outcomes through evidence-based care. Working collaboratively with physicians, nurses, and other healthcare professionals, the Lactation Consultant supports patients across the perinatal continuum while advancing patient-centered, family-focused care in a leading academic medical center. Location: University Hospital (0870) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 36 Shift: Second Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Ohio-State-Student-Farm-Production-Coordinator_R154360-2": {
      "title": "Ohio State Student Farm Production Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Ohio State Student Farm Production Coordinator Department: FAES | Horticulture and Crop Science The Department of Horticulture and Crop Science at The Ohio State University is seeking applications for the position of Student Farm Production Coordinator 3. This is a full-time, year-round position. The Production Manager is the primary farmer responsible for growing vegetables, fruits, and flowers using a combination of row-crop, plasticulture and intensive bed production methods on 4 acres including high tunnel, open field, and greenhouse. This position will be assisted by seasonal volunteers and part-time co-workers, primarily OSU undergraduate students interested in being involved with the Student Farm.  Responsibilities Field •    Seed, transplant, and cultivate row crops using tractors, hand-tools, and implements. •    Lead and manage seasonal volunteers and part-time co-workers.  •    Maintain timely tillage seedbed preparation with the help of Waterman Farm Operation. •    Manage plant disease, pests, and irrigation through scouting, drip irrigation system, overhead traveler irrigation system, row cover, and successive planting. •    Scout fields and collaborate with the sales operation regarding crop scheduling, anticipated harvest dates, and yields. •    Safely operate tractors, trucks, and various implements; supported with training. •    Learn and follow routine equipment maintenance procedures, along with minor repair, report damage and repair needs. Tunnels, Intensive Beds and Greenhouses •    Plan, coordinate and oversee crop production in intensive beds, low tunnels, and high tunnels using walk-behind tractor and implements, hand tools.  •    Greenhouse production of transplants including germination chambers. •    Maintain the high tunnels by making necessary repairs as needed, coordinating venting and helping to remove snow as needed. Administrative •    Use of Excel/Google Sheets/Qualtrics for planning, mapping, and distributing information. •    Order seeds and document purchases. •    Maintain and oversee maintenance of accurate records. •    Keep current with the latest production and harvest practices for a wide range of vegetables. •    Maintain compliance with food safety standards in accordance with Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) •    Coordinate on class activities/practicum sessions that can take place or engage with the student farm. This includes but is not limited to HCS 2307 Sustainable Agriculture Practical Experience (Fall) and HCS 2306 Sustainable Vegetable Production Practicum (Spring). •    Engage with potential donors interested in supporting the student farm.  •    Lead monthly newsletter publication on updates about the farm and summary of relevant information for small scale and vegetable farmers.   •    Support writing materials (grans application, extension article, peer review publications) related to the efforts of the student farm.   •    Be motivated to adapt to changing roles as this position develops over seasons. Supervising/Mentoring  •    Supervise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students conducting activities at the farm.  •    Supervise seasonal volunteers and part-time co-workers.  Required Attributes •    Positive attitude and desire to meet high expectations. •    Dependable, reliable, consistent, and on time, ready to work. •    Self-starter with the ability to manage multiple priorities. •    Team leader: motivate, inspire, and get results. •    Committed to improving management skills and leadership mindset. •    Skillful with interpersonal relations. •    Active problem-solver. •    Planful, with flexibility to respond to changing circumstances and expectations. •    Polite, empathic, and professional attitude and manner. •    Active listener and excellent communicator. •    Detail oriented. •    Organized. •    Committed to a quality product. Qualifications •    The minimum qualification for this position is a high school diploma/GED and 2 years of relevant experience. the preferred qualifications for this position is an earned BS in horticulture or plant science, agronomy or soil science, sustainable agriculture, agroecology, or discipline applicable to the duties and responsibilities outlined above.  •    Technological skills: capable of using computer/tablet/smartphone with Google, Qualtrics, & Microsoft Office applications for real-time updates in the field. •    Driver’s license valid in OH. •    Experience using tractors, implements, walk-behind tractors, and hand tools. •    Communicate in English. Foundational Farming Context •    This position requires some flexibility, with a willingness to adjust schedules around weather to get each week’s jobs completed. •    In turn, this position offers some flexibility in work days and start/stop times relative to the seasons and needs of the crops. •    Ability to work in all weather conditions including precipitation, heat, humidity and cold. Compensation and Benefits •    Comprehensive Benefit Package •     Salary range $16.65 - $21.77 hourly commensurate with experience, education and internal equity •    Professional development (conference attendance, grad student symposium plant science symposium).  •    Gain experience working in the commercial production and sales of food products. Additional Information: This job profile is a Farm Coordinator 3 (T3 level) on the career roadmap. Location: Waterman - Laboratory Headquarters (0179) Position Type: Term (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/College-of-MedicineOffice-of-Health-Sciences/Education-Program-Specialist-3---CTSI_R157216-1": {
      "title": "Education Program Specialist 3 - CTSI",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Education Program Specialist 3 - CTSI Department: Health Sciences | Clinical and Translational Science Institute Position Summary The Education Program Specialist 3 supports the administration, coordination, and evaluation of CTSI’s Investigator Career Development programs. Reporting to the Associate Director for Investigator Development, this role ensures timely communication, coordination, and monitoring of high-quality remote and in-person educational workshops, training opportunities, and career development initiatives for graduate students, residents, fellows, and junior faculty. The Education Program Specialist 3 works closely with CTSI leadership, faculty, staff, and trainees/scholars to manage day-to-day program operations and contribute to long-term program improvement. Key Responsibilities Program Coordination & Delivery Coordinate the scheduling and promotion of recurring educational series, workshops, and events, including: Monthly Seminar Series Mentoring workshops (3/year) Career Dinners (3/year) Thematic or topical workshops Grant-writing workshops Grant writing office hours to support grant development through one-on-one advising Other related meetings and events as required Support new externship initiatives and career development opportunities. Develop and maintain training and program communication resources (e.g., video libraries, online modules). Grant Administration & Compliance Assist with administrative responsibilities for NIH and institutional training grants. Coordinate and monitor trainee/scholar appointment processes, OSU HR requirements, and NIH xTrain submissions. Ensure compliance with NIH and university reporting requirements. Evaluation & Reporting Maintain surveys for relevance and conduct pre- and post-program assessments, mentoring surveys, and annual evaluations. Coordinate, collect, and monitor trainee/scholar progress updates through Individual Development Plans (IDPs), mentoring plans, and program milestones. Collect, analyze, and report data for internal stakeholders, NIH progress reports, and institutional updates. Use tools such as the Flight Tracker to monitor career trajectories and program outcomes. Establish and manage a database to track junior faculty outcomes (e.g., publications, presentations, patents, funding, novel treatments/therapeutics), benchmarking results against national data. Help support and maintain project plans and Smartsheet to reflect accurate grant and project status Collaboration & Continuous Improvement Work closely with the Associate Director and CTSI evaluation team to assess and enhance program effectiveness. Contribute to program development by identifying opportunities for new initiatives and process improvements. Assist with promotional activities to raise awareness of CTSI education and training programs. Minimim Requirements Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. An advanced degree in a relevant field is desirable. 4 years of relevant experience required. 4-8 years of relevant experience preferred. Additional Information: Location: Prior Hall (0302) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Health-System-Shared-Services/Manager--Nursing-Business-Operations_R157504-1": {
      "title": "Manager, Nursing Business Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Manager, Nursing Business Operations Department: James | Business Operations Scope of Position The Manager, Nursing Business Operations oversees business operations and administrative oversight of the Nursing Business Office supporting all Nursing units (the “Nursing Department”) across the Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center (“OSUWMC”). The Manager is responsible for identifying financial issues and implementing improvements that will enhance the organization’s profitability. The Manager, in collaboration with other key stakeholders (Finance and Nursing Leadership), is accountable for developing the annual budget for the Nursing Department and tracking on-going financial performance to those targets throughout the year. The Manager provides business analytic support and in-sights to Senior Leadership (Nursing, Finance, and Executive Directors) to allow data-driven decision making. The Manager supervises, develops, and evaluates the Nursing Business Operations staff. The Manager reports to the James Director of Business Operations. Position Summary The Manager, Nursing Business Operations leads the business and administrative operations of the Nursing Business Office. The Manager provides oversight in developing and translating the financial budget and fiscal year objectives of the Nursing Department into action and achievement. The Manager helps oversee business transactions, expense management, and financial operations of the Nursing Department. The Manager establishes and maintains systems for reporting key performance metrics that monitor and report the overall performance and throughput of the clinical operations of the Nursing Department, and provides consultation and education to the Chief Nursing Officers and other Nursing Leadership. The Manager collaborates across OSUWMC on system-wide analyses and initiatives to promote cohesiveness and the effective utilization of system resources to achieve organization goals and objectives. Minimum Qualifications For Hire: Bachelor’s degree in business administration, finance, accounting, or applicable field, or equivalent experience. Advanced degree preferred. Minimum 5 years of relevant professional experience required. Ability to work in matrix environment and provide team leadership across reporting and departmental lines. Administrative management with relevant hospital operations experience desired. Experience with financial and data visualization systems (Tableau), Microsoft Office programs, including Word, Excel, Power Point, Access or other database applications are essential. Experience with financial, clinical data, and business information systems is highly desirable. Effective verbal and written communication skills are essential. Ongoing:  Maintain licensure (if applicable). Demonstrated competency to meet essential job functions. Ongoing participation in professional organizations that provide continuing educational opportunities and promote professional advancement.  Demonstrated ability to function as an interdisciplinary team member who actively contributes to the effective planning, coordination, and implementation of healthcare services to meet the needs of the patients, families and community served. Career Roadmap: FUNCTION: Business Planning and Operations SUB-FUNCTION: Business Operations CAREER BAND: People Leader - Managerial CAREER LEVEL: M2 Additional Information: Location: Ackerman Rd, 660 (0242) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/James-Cancer-Hospital-and-Solove-Research-Institute/Nursing-Professional-Development-Practitioner---Operating-Room_R150481-1": {
      "title": "Nursing Professional Development Practitioner (Nursing Educator) - Operating Room",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Nursing Professional Development Practitioner (Nursing Educator) - Operating Room Department: James | Nursing Staff Education Scope of Position : The Nursing Professional Development (NPD) practitioner provides ongoing and constant support to the transforming healthcare landscape. The NPD practitioner functions as a nurse leader in an interprofessional environment applying evidenced based practice, clinical expertise, and patient values to improve patient outcomes. The NPD practitioner engages in environmental scanning to continuously assess potential professional practice gaps. By using various sources of data, the NPD practitioner identifies learning needs that include but are not limited to emerging issues, new or updated evidenced based guidelines, comparison of current performance and/or outcomes with national data bases and use of new tools and techniques.   Position Summary : The NPD practitioner is a master’s prepared registered nurse who influences professional role competence and professional growth of learners in a variety of settings. This NPD practitioner maintains lifelong learners in an interprofessional setting that facilitates continuous development and learning for the healthcare team. The NPD practitioner demonstrates expertise in the identified roles: learning facilitator, change agent, mentor, leader, champion for scientific inquiry, advocate for NPD specialty and partner for practice transitions. Responsibilities include: onboarding/orientation, competency management, education, professional role development, collaborative partnerships, research, evidenced based practice and quality improvement.   Minimum Qualifications:  Masters Degree in Nursing or Bachelors Degree in Nursing AND masters in related field (i.e. MHA, Nursing Education, etc). Two years of nursing experience is required.  Current Ohio RN license required. Additional Information: Location: James Cancer Hospital (0375) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Dodd-Rehabilitation-Hospital/Staff-Nurse--RN----Acute-Inpatient-Rehabilitation_R150423": {
      "title": "Staff Nurse (RN) - Acute Inpatient Rehabilitation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Staff Nurse (RN) - Acute Inpatient Rehabilitation Department: University Hospital | 3 Dodd Hall, Brain and Spinal Cord Injury Rehabilitation Scope of Position: The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center’s mission is to improve health in Ohio and across the world through innovation in research, education, and patient care. The team provides patient care and supportive services directed towards achievement of positive patient care outcomes, maximizing the patient’s involvement in his/her own plan of care and reducing the length of hospitalization, The staff nurse plays a critical role in staff engagement, the patient experience, quality and safety, and cost-effective care. Position Summary: The Staff Nurse is responsible for managing and providing care to the patient and his/her family, and for directing and supervising nursing care provided by other members of the patient care team. The Staff Nurse is responsible for assessing, planning, implementing, coordinating, delegating and evaluating the nursing care of patients in alignment with the professional practice model.  Minimum Qualifications For Hire:   2- year College Degree in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program is required.   Bachelor’s degree in nursing with a major in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program is preferred. Current Ohio license or interim permit required. 2 years of experience in rehabilitation or acute care setting is preferred. ​ On-going:  Maintains current Ohio RN license. Meets mandatory educational and health requirements.  Demonstrates computer skills required to meet job functions. Additional Information: The Acute Inpatient Rehabilitation Unit on the third floor of Dodd Hospital provides comprehensive rehab care for individuals 16+ with brain injury, spinal cord injury, and oncology diagnoses. The unit is supported by an interdisciplinary team and maintains a strong focus on staff and patient safety, clinical excellence, and professional growth. This role offers the opportunity to build advanced rehabilitation expertise while working in a Magnet-recognized, CARF-accredited environment that prioritizes safety, teamwork, and continuous professional development. *Day or night shift available Staffing & Care Model Nurse-to-patient ratio: 1:5, with flexibility to 1:4 for high-acuity rehabilitation patients High-acuity care may include telemetry, continuous pulse oximetry, infectious workups, and care for complex medical needs Emphasis on patient and caregiver education and coordinated, team-based care   Clinical Skills Utilized RNs on this unit routinely apply broad acute care skills, including: Tracheostomy management Wound care, including wound VACs and burn dressings Intermittent catheterization and bowel programs Line and port management   Safety & Accreditation Robust ergonomic support: ceiling lifts in all patient rooms, floor lifts, transfer devices, shower chairs, stand-assist devices, slide boards, and more Magnet® Hospital, achieving a fifth re-designation in 2025 CARF-accredited specialty areas: Comprehensive Inpatient Rehabilitation Program, Brain Injury Program, Spinal Cord Injury Program, Stroke Program, and Oncology Program Growth Opportunities Flexible scheduling to support work–life balance and school commitments Clinical ladder and specialty certification support Opportunities to serve on committees and participate in professional organizations, including COARN (local) and ARN (national) Location: Dodd Hall (0171) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 36 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Harding-Hospital/Staff-Nurse--RN----Inpatient-Psychiatry-Float-Pool_R150682": {
      "title": "Staff Nurse (RN) - Inpatient Psychiatry Float Pool",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Staff Nurse (RN) - Inpatient Psychiatry Float Pool Department: Harding | 4NP Adult Inpatient Psychiatry Scope of Position: The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center’s mission is to improve health in Ohio and across the world through innovation in research, education, and patient care. The team provides patient care and supportive services directed towards achievement of positive patient care outcomes, maximizing the patient’s involvement in his/her own plan of care and reducing the length of hospitalization, The staff nurse plays a critical role in staff engagement, the patient experience, quality and safety, and cost-effective care. Position Summary: The Staff Nurse is responsible for managing and providing care to the patient and his/her family, and for directing and supervising nursing care provided by other members of the patient care team. The Staff Nurse is responsible for assessing, planning, implementing, coordinating, delegating and evaluating the nursing care of patients in alignment with the professional practice model.  Minimum Qualifications For Hire:   2- year College Degree in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program is required.   Bachelor’s degree in nursing with a major in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program is preferred. Current Ohio license or interim permit required. 2 years of experience in behavioral or acute care setting is preferred. ​ On-going:  Maintains current Ohio RN license. Meets mandatory educational and health requirements.  Demonstrates computer skills required to meet job functions. Additional Information: Harding Hospital at the OSU Wexner Medical Center offers adult and geriatric in-patient program with 84 beds and provides emergency stabilization, diagnosis and the initial stages of treatment for those requiring inpatient care. Patient-centered, trauma-informed care is supported by an interdisciplinary team with a strong focus on staff and patient safety, clinical excellence, and professional growth.   Harding Float Pool staff supports 84 inpatient beds across 4 psychiatric units with varying adult populations with diagnoses ranging from schizoaffective/ schizophrenia to mood disorders to anxiety. Location: Harding Hospital (0165) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 36 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
