    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/East-Hospital/Med-Lab-Tech-Processing---IRP---East-Laboratory_R157617-1": {
      "title": "Med Lab Tech-Processing - IRP - East Laboratory",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Med Lab Tech-Processing - IRP - East Laboratory Department: East | Laboratory Scope of Position         The East Clinical Laboratory encompasses specimen processing and testing services within the Department of Clinical Laboratories including client services and all areas within the Rapid Response Laboratory.  The laboratory is staffed 24 hours per day, including Saturday and Sunday.   Position Summary       The medical laboratory technician-processor (MLT-Processor) is responsible for covering the duties and responsibilities of the Central Processing area and/or Microb9iology processing area within the department of Clinical Laboratories.  The MLT-Processor performs specimen processing, manual computer test order entry, verification of laboratory test requisition entry, and customer service related duties.  The MLT-Processor also participates in quality control, continuous quality improvement activities, inventory control, professional development and continuing education within the area.    Minimum Qualifications   For Hire:          High School diploma or GED.  Certification or vocational training may be required.      On going:       Meets mandatory hospital education and health surveillance requirements. Demonstrates competence annually in technical, interpersonal, and cognitive skills required to meet essential job functions . Additional Information: Minimum Qualifications For Hire: High School diploma or GED.  Certification or vocational training may be required. On going: Meets mandatory hospital education and health surveillance requirements. Demonstrates competence annually in technical, interpersonal, and cognitive skills required to meet essential job functions . Location: East Hospital - Main (0398) Position Type: Intermittent Scheduled Hours: 0.2 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Intermediate-Application-Developer_R157663-1": {
      "title": "Intermediate Application Developer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Intermediate Application Developer Department: OTDI | Mobile and Web Applications The Application Developer provides technical expertise for the development, integration, and support of enterprise applications within Application Services. Reporting to the Application Development Team Lead, this role implements software solutions using scalable, secure, and maintainable engineering practices aligned with established architectural standards and development governance.   Application Services designs, builds, integrates, and sustains long-lived enterprise applications supporting core institutional operations. The Application Developer contributes to the development and enhancement of enterprise web, API, mobile, and cloud-enabled applications while applying disciplined software development lifecycle practices and engineering quality standards.   This role serves as a developing technical contributor within the development team, executing implementation efforts, participating in technical design discussions, and applying established engineering practices with growing independence across development initiatives.   The Application Developer supports the long-term sustainability of enterprise applications by writing maintainable code, contributing to reliable system behavior, and applying disciplined engineering practices across development work.   Required Education and Experience:   Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Systems, or equivalent combination of education and experience.   2 years of experience in enterprise application development.   Demonstrated experience developing and supporting software solutions.   Experience working with modern software development lifecycle practices.   Experience writing maintainable and scalable application code.   Experience with source control, CI/CD pipelines, and automated testing.   Experience integrating with applications using REST APIs, event-driven architectures, or middleware platforms.   Demonstrated ability to leverage AI tools to accelerate software delivery while applying critical thinking and engineering best practices.   Willingness to continuously evaluate and adopt emerging AI capabilities as part of the software development process.   Strong written and verbal communication skills suitable for technical collaboration.   Desired Education and Experience:   2-4 years of experience in enterprise application development.   Experience participating in technical design and architecture discussions.   Experience developing applications in cloud-enabled environments.   Familiarity with enterprise integration patterns and API development.   Experience with serverless architectures, containerized applications, or cloud-native integration services.   Experience with reactJS   Experience with Infrastructure as Code.   Experience working with AI orchestration and MCP servers.   Experience supporting enterprise applications in large, decentralized institutions.   Additional Information: The salary range for this position is $70,100-$91,600 and the offer for this position will be based on internal equity and the candidate's qualifications.   Function: Information Technology Sub-function: Enterprise Application Development Career Band: Specialized Career Level: S2 Location: Mount Hall (0311) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
