    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Housing-Operations-Coordinator_R157858-1": {
      "title": "Housing Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Housing Operations Coordinator Department: Student Life | Columbus Housing and Residence Education The Housing Operations Coordinator functions as an integral member of the Housing and Residence Education (HRE) team. HRE is comprised of over 60 full-time staff members, 20 graduate and 800 undergraduate student staff members. The staff support over 16,000 residential students on 4 campuses. Reporting to the Assistant Director in HRE Housing Services, this position provides broad leadership and independent decision making in processing financial transactions related to housing contracts and assignments; completing and submitting accurate and detailed financial transaction statements for payments submitted via check and credit card; processing completed contracts; reviewing requests and communicating decisions regarding Emotional Support Animals (ESAs) and Service/Assistance Animals in compliance with ADA/HUD standards and guidelines in partnership with The Ohio State University Student Life Disability Services Office and ADA Coordinator Office; managing assignment information in the department’s housing occupancy management software related to room/assignment changes; anticipating, recognizing, and solving complex issues and concerns that arise with our customers while staying in compliance with University procedures and expectations regarding the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA), Payment Card Compliance (PCI), Institutional Data Policy (IDP), and Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act. The Housing Operations Coordinator is responsible for processing in person and over the phone credit card payments; ensuring student billing is reflective of their Tuition Guarantee cohort requiring extensive understanding of the cohort structures and impacts on student fees; responding to inquiries or concerns submitted to the Housing and Residence Education departmental email account; assisting in training student and full-time staff on processes and procedures related to room changes, contract information with deadlines, and the University On Campus Housing Regulation (Columbus and Wooster/ATI Campuses); communicates with students, faculty, staff and parents regarding contractual Terms and Conditions; serves as a point of contact and liaison between Housing Services and Student Life Financial Management, Student Life Facilities, Environmental Services, Student Life Disability Services, and other campus partners, and routinely works and communicates effectively with the Housing and Residence Education Administrative Coordinators, Hall Directors, and Assistant Hall Directors. QUALIFICATIONS Required: High School diploma or GED. 2 years of relevant experience required Desires: Associate degree in relevant field. 4 or more years of relevant experience Additional Information: PAY RANGE: $16.65 to $21.77 The offer for this position will fall within this range based on internal equity, the unit’s available budget, and the selected candidate’s qualifications. Career Roadmap Designation https://hr.osu.edu/career-roadmap/ Function: Student Life Sub Function: Housing and Residence Life Career Level: T3 The Office of Student Life fosters students’ development, learning, well-being and sense of belonging; empowers students to achieve their academic, personal and professional goals; and prepares students to be engaged in a global society. Location: Lincoln Tower (0271) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Housing-Operations-Lead-Coordinator_R157849-1": {
      "title": "Housing Operations Lead Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Housing Operations Lead Coordinator Department: Student Life | Columbus Housing and Residence Education The Housing Operations Lead Coordinator functions as an integral member of the Housing and Residence Education (HRE) team. HRE is comprised of over 60 full-time staff members, 20 graduate and 800 undergraduate student staff members. The staff support over 16,000 residential students on 4 campuses. Reporting to the Assistant Director in HRE Housing Services, this position provides broad leadership and independent decision making in processing financial transactions related to housing contracts and assignments; completing and submitting accurate and detailed financial transaction statements for payments submitted via check and credit card; processing completed contracts; reviewing requests and communicating decisions regarding Emotional Support Animals (ESAs) and Service/Assistance Animals in compliance with ADA/HUD standards and guidelines in partnership with The Ohio State University Student Life Disability Services Office and ADA Coordinator Office; managing assignment information in the department’s housing occupancy management software related to room/assignment changes; anticipating, recognizing, and solving complex issues and concerns that arise with our customers while staying in compliance with University procedures and expectations regarding the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA), Payment Card Compliance (PCI), Institutional Data Policy (IDP), and Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act. The Housing Operations Lead Coordinator is responsible for processing in person and over the phone credit card payments; ensuring student billing is reflective of their Tuition Guarantee cohort requiring extensive understanding of the cohort structures and impacts on student fees; responding to inquiries or concerns submitted to the Housing and Residence Education departmental email account; assisting in training student and full-time staff on processes and procedures related to room changes, contract information with deadlines, and the University On Campus Housing Regulation (Columbus and Wooster/ATI Campuses); communicates with students, faculty, staff and parents regarding contractual Terms and Conditions; serves as a point of contact and liaison between Housing Services and Student Life Financial Management, Student Life Facilities, Environmental Services, Student Life Disability Services, and other campus partners, and routinely works and communicates effectively with the Housing and Residence Education Administrative Coordinators, Hall Directors, and Assistant Hall Directors. QUALIFICATIONS Required: High School diploma or GED. 4 years of relevant experience required. Desired: Associate degree in relevant field. 6 or more years of relevant experience. Additional Information: PAY RANGE $18.37 to $23.99 The offer for this position will fall within this range based on internal equity, the unit’s available budget, and the selected candidate’s qualifications. Career Roadmap Designation https://hr.osu.edu/career-roadmap/ Function: Student Life Sub Function: Housing and Residence Life Career Level: T4 MISSION The Office of Student Life fosters students’ development, learning, well-being and sense of belonging; empowers students to achieve their academic, personal and professional goals; and prepares students to be engaged in a global society. Location: Lincoln Tower (0271) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/PharmD-Recruitment-and-Admissions-Specialist_R157782-2": {
      "title": "PharmD Recruitment and Admissions Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: PharmD Recruitment and Admissions Specialist Department: Pharmacy | Professional Studies Under the leadership of the Assistant Director for Recruitment and Admissions, the PharmD Admissions Recruiter represents The Ohio State University College of Pharmacy through daily interactions and communications with prospective and newly matriculated  students, as well as provides support throughout the application and admissions process. The PharmD Admissions Recruiter creates and implements recruitment strategies to reach prospective students through events, referrals, online and print communications, and outreach to pharmacy professionals and organizations. The PharmD Admissions Recruiter will be responsible for planning admissions and yield events which may include but are not limited to PharmD overviews, application workshops, calling campaigns, postcard campaigns, and university-sponsored and off-campus events which will require travel. The PharmD Admissions Recruiter is responsible for scheduling and planning PharmD interview days and plays a critical role in the day-of management of these events. This position works closely with the faculty-composed Admissions Committee, communicating admissions information, garnering recruitment event support, and acting as a liaison between candidates and the committee's decisions. This role conducts initial application review; moves applicants through the recruitment pipeline; and communicates admission decisions. This position oversees the PharmD Student Ambassador Program, including the management of approximately 3 PharmD student ambassador coordinators; and facilitates the recruitment, selection, and activities of ~35 student admissions ambassadors. This position supports various initiatives and programs within the Office of Recruitment and Admissions. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. A minimum of 2 years working within higher education; experience working with graduate or professional students; student supervision experience; experience developing and implementing best practices in recruitment and admissions; able to manage multiple priorities; and strong written and verbal communication skills. Desired Qualifications: Master’s degree in Higher Education, College Student Personnel or related field. Additional Information: The pay range for this job profile is $20.24 - $26.44 per hour. The offer for this position will fall within this range based on internal equity, unit's available budget, and the candidate's qualifications.   The College of Pharmacy believes in a healthy work/life balance, therefore, the work arrangement for this position is hybrid (i.e., remote and in-office), subject to change based upon the needs of the organization and as determined by College Leadership.   FUNCTION: Academic Administration SUBFUNCTION: Graduate and Professional Admissions CAREER BAND: Specialized CAREER LEVEL: S2 Location: Parks Hall (0273) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Senior-Career-Counselor_R157592-1": {
      "title": "Senior Career Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Senior Career Counselor Department: Pharmacy | Academic Affairs Under the leadership of the Senior Director for Student Success in the College of Pharmacy Academic Affairs unit, the Senior Career Counselor is primarily responsible for the development and execution of student-centered career development and services for PharmD and graduate students. The Senior Career Counselor will strategically lead career-related activities by engaging with college and external stakeholders to identify professional, and graduate students unique needs to create and maintain career-related resources. This role is also responsible for serving as the liaison with departments and across the university. The specialist will also lead the development and management of employer relations, as well as the planning and implementation of career fairs and other career services- related events. In addition, this position will provide career advising to PharmD and graduate students in the college through individual appointments as well as presentations and also develop, execute, and evaluate the career-focused curricular and co-curricular courses, content, and programming. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience. At least 4 years of experience working with career focused programs and students. Desired Qualifications: Master’s degree in higher education, student affairs/personnel, or related field is desired due to teaching responsibilities of position. Familiarity with employment landscape for pharmacy and pharmaceutical sciences. Additional Information: The pay range for this job profile is $51,500 - $67,250. The offer for this position will fall within this range based on internal equity, unit's available budget, and the candidate's qualifications.   The College of Pharmacy believes in a healthy work/life balance, therefore, the work arrangement for this position is hybrid (i.e., remote and in-office), subject to change based upon the needs of the organization and as determined by College Leadership.   FUNCTION: Academic Administration SUBFUNCTION: Career Services CAREER BAND: Specialized CAREER LEVEL: S3 Location: Parks Hall (0273) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
