    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Senior-Information-Systems-Auditor_R157826-1": {
      "title": "Senior Information Systems Auditor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Senior Information Systems Auditor Department: Business and Finance | Internal Audit The Department of Internal Audit is responsible for performing audits and consulting activities on key University risks and critical processes. The Department accomplishes this by creating and maintaining strong relationships with University and Wexner Medical Center personnel and fostering collaboration to help achieve the University’s goals. The Department is broken down into three teams (University, Health System, and Information Technology). The Information Technology (IT) team performs audits at both the University and Wexner Medical Center as well as at the University’s affiliated entities. The Senior Information Systems (IS) Auditor will perform independent IS audits and multi-disciplinary reviews for the university community (Wexner Medical Center, academic areas, central operations, etc.), identifying risks for the many separate companies that exist under the university umbrella; assists management in effective discharge of responsibilities by performing independent audits and furnishing analyses, appraisals, recommendations, counsel, and information concerning activities reviewed; performs audits in accordance with audit plans and Institute of Internal Auditor Standards; prepares oral/written presentations; discusses observations and recommendations; performs IS audits and multi-disciplinary reviews (i.e. technology, financial, operational, and advisory projects) across the University; obtains, documents, and analyzes evidentiary data as a basis to form an opinion on adequacy of internal controls and compliance with policies, procedures, laws and regulations; attends and participates in oral presentations; prepares written reports; performs follow-up reviews; assists in supervision of staff auditors. The position reports to the Associate Director, IS Audit, in a unit that enjoys a strong reputation across campus. Professional development opportunities for the selected individual include certifications, training, professional membership, and rewards for continued education. Due to the nature of the work, this role may be performed in a hybrid working environment with a typical schedule of Monday through Friday, regular business hours with few requests to work more than a 40-hour workweek. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's Level Degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum four (4) years information systems audit experience in technology- based tools or methodologies to review various technologies, networks, security systems, software applications, interfaces, authentication processes, etc.; strong analytical and communication skills; experience conducting general controls, application controls and IT security reviews; knowledge of systems development life cycle and project management. Desired Qualifications: Certification or progress towards certification as a Certified Information Systems Auditor (CISA), Certified Public Accountant (CPA), or Certified Internal Auditor (CIA). Function: Finance Sub-function: Information Systems Internal Audit Career Band: Individual Contributor – Specialized Career Level: S3 Additional Information: The Target Hiring Range for this position is $81,800 to $106,900 per year. Ohio State will not sponsor applicants for work visas for this position.  Location: Student Academic Services (0160) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Newark-Campus/Undergraduate-Academic-Advisor-2--Newark-_R157827-1": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Academic Advisor 2 (Newark)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Undergraduate Academic Advisor 2 (Newark) Department: Newark | General The Ohio State University Newark campus serves undergraduate students pursuing any of the university’s 200+ majors, including several degree programs that can be completed entirely at Newark. The Undergraduate Academic Advisor 2 position provides academic advising and support to students within a designated group of undergraduate majors. The Undergraduate Academic Advisor 2 plays a key role in promoting student success through proactive advising practices that help students make informed decisions and stay on track toward degree completion. This position provides individualized academic advising, assisting students with course planning and selection based on their academic progress, personal interests, and career goals. The advisor helps students understand and navigate university policies, degree requirements, academic procedures, and institutional expectations. In addition, the Undergraduate Academic Advisor 2 connects students with a wide range of campus resources designed to support their academic achievement and overall well-being, including tutoring and academic support services, career development resources, financial assistance programs, and mental health and wellness services. Working with a moderate level of independence, the Undergraduate Academic Advisor 2 completes structured assignments and contributes to projects of varying complexity. The position applies advanced advising concepts, established practices, and technical knowledge to support student needs and departmental objectives. The advisor communicates information on routine and standard matters, collaborating with colleagues and receiving guidance from senior staff when appropriate. Success in this role requires a strong understanding of academic advising principles, student development theory, and higher education practices gained through education and professional experience. Additional responsibilities include supporting new student orientation programs by preparing materials and delivering presentations to students and their families as needed. The Undergraduate Academic Advisor 2 also facilitates lessons within a student survey course using established curriculum and instructional materials, participates in professional development and training activities, and may evaluate and grade student assignments. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong academic advising skills, a commitment to student learning and development, excellent interpersonal and communication abilities, and a collaborative approach to supporting student success. Responsibilities: Academic Advising and Student Support Provide and document individualized academic advising for undergraduate students regarding degree and program options, academic standards, General Education requirements, prerequisite coursework, and major-specific requirements. Consult with or escalate complex student issues to senior advising staff as appropriate. Assist students in navigating university processes and connect them with campus resources that support academic success, career development, financial well-being, and mental health. Advise students experiencing academic difficulty, including those on academic probation. Review and process academic transactions, including course adds/drops, withdrawals, and program changes. Orientation Support New student orientation programs by assisting with the preparation of orientation materials and resources. Present information to students, parents, and family members during orientation sessions as needed. Projects, Teaching, and Professional Development Under general direction, participate in and occasionally lead special projects that support departmental and campus objectives. Identify opportunities for process improvements or new initiatives and provide recommendations to management. Engage in ongoing professional development and participate in unit- and university-wide training and development opportunities. Contribute input to the Newark campus course schedule to help ensure that course offerings meet student degree and program requirements. Teach lessons in the university survey course and may independently instruct specialized course sections. Use established curriculum and instructional materials, making only minor modifications as needed to effectively deliver content. Attend required training sessions, grade student assignments as assigned, and assist with the review and updating of course materials. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree or 2+ years of equivalent experience (Master’s required for teaching). Years of relevant experience required: 0. Preferred Qualifications Preferred minimum years of relevant experience: 1-2 Ability to explain complex information in a clear and student-friendly manner. Strong communication skills, with the ability to effectively convey program requirements to diverse audiences, including students, parents, faculty, and campus partners. Demonstrated understanding of multiculturalism, inclusion, and best practices for supporting diverse student populations. Proficiency in performing routine transactions and navigating the Student Information System (SIS). Strong interpersonal skills, including active listening, effective interviewing, and thoughtful questioning techniques. Knowledge of and commitment to maintaining student privacy and confidentiality in accordance with FERPA guidelines. This position is based at the Ohio State University, Newark Campus in Newark, Ohio, with a target hiring range of $45,000 to $51,000 Additional Information: The College The Ohio State University at Newark offered its first classes in 1957 with a mission to provide affordable, open access to Ohio State for all Ohioans. The Newark campus sits on 188 acres and shares the campus with Central Ohio Technical College. The two institutions have a strong partnership whereby they share all buildings and general-purpose classrooms, approximately 100 staff, operating expenses, and a number of capital equipment investments. Shared departments include Advancement; Business and Finance; Facilities, Planning and Operations; Library; Marketing and Public Relations; Purchasing and Auxiliary Services; Student Financial Services; and Student Life.  Ohio State Newark currently enrolls more than 2,200 students who are taught and mentored by 45 tenure-track faculty who are members of their university-level academic department. Students can complete eight bachelor’s degree programs at the Newark Campus and start any of Ohio State’s 200+ majors. In addition to excellent academic offerings, students can participate in the Honors program, service learning, education abroad, and a wide variety of student clubs and organizations.   Ohio State Newark is situated near the Ohio State University Columbus campus, presenting great opportunities for new and innovative partnerships to benefit students, faculty, and staff. The future of the campus will be impacted by the significant growth and development in Licking County, including a new Intel facility, expansion of Meta and Google facilities, and more. Students are creating innovative pathways to their degree completion due to the proximity to multiple campuses.  Location: Hodges Hall (0628) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/James-Cancer-Hospital-and-Solove-Research-Institute/Physical-Therapist_R157503-2": {
      "title": "Physical Therapist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Physical Therapist Department: James | Rehabilitation Services Acute Care The Physical Therapist evaluates and treats patients in accordance with the laws and rules that govern the practice of physical therapy in the state of Ohio. Although team members report directly to a team leader, they are also responsible to each other, to those they supervise ( and to other participants included in the patient care activities. Minimum Qualifications Physical Therapist   rehabilitation team members must be licensed or certified with the respective profession (physical therapy), and meet the educational and/or certification requirements established by their professions (physical therapist must hold a minimum of a bachelor’s degree). All academic degrees must have been granted from an accredited institution.  Typically, one-two years’ experience working in a medical setting is preferred for all professionals hired.  New graduates will be considered if they have completed a majority of their clinical work in this setting.. Maintains professional licensure; demonstrates commitment to continuing education; meets mandatory education and health requirements; demonstrates competence in technical, interpersonal, and cognitive skills required to meet essential job functions   Additional Information: Location: James Cancer Hospital (0375) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Outpatient-CareAmbulatory/Research-Aide-and-Interviewer_R151639-1": {
      "title": "Research Aide and Interviewer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Research Aide and Interviewer Department: Medicine | Otolaryngology The university will not sponsor applicants for work visas for this position and applicants must be enrolled in a US medical school in good academic standing. The Research Technician provides entry‑level technical support for scientific investigations related to their chosen primary mentor from a list of approved NIH funded faculty within the Department of Otolaryngology – Head and Neck Surgery . Working under clearly established guidelines and with close guidance from the supervisor and experienced team members, the individual performs routine laboratory procedures such as PCR, gel electrophoresis, basic assays, and cell culture, and assists with processing tissue and blood samples. Responsibilities include maintaining accurate laboratory records, preparing materials and equipment for experiments, monitoring supplies, and supporting day‑to‑day lab operations. The individual collects and organizes data, solves straightforward technical problems, and contributes to research activities by following structured work assignments. Interaction is primarily with the immediate supervisor and lab team, with limited independent discretion. Additional support may include assisting with animal procedures, basic literature searches, and helping orient new students or staff to simple lab tasks Minimum Education & Experience Required A pplicants must be enrolled in a US medical school in good academic standing. Requires successful completion of a background check; qualified candidates may be asked to complete a pre-employment physical, including a drug screen. Additional Information: Location: Eye and Ear Institute (0897) Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Health-System-Shared-Services/Home-Hospital-RN_R137802-1": {
      "title": "Home Hospital RN - IRP/Contingent",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Home Hospital RN - IRP/Contingent Department: Shared Services | Post-Acute and Home Based Care Services Hospital Care at Home is an innovative care model that allows us to provide inpatient level care to patients in their homes. Potential patients are assessed by a Home Hospital provider to ensure their diagnosis can be treated in the home, that the patient’s home environment is a safe place to receive care, and that the patient has consented to participate. We have successfully cared for more than 500 patients in Hospital Care at Home and are excited to continue to grow! The Home Hospital RN will partner closely with the attending physician and other members of the care team to provide care for patients, both virtually and through in-home visits. Primary responsibilities include: Participate in the initial and ongoing assessment of patients determining care and services needed to stay in the home. Collaborate with medical providers, patient care staff and skilled services in the planning and implementation of patient care plan. Direct and coordinate services (i.e., nursing, therapy, care management, etc.) provided in the home during the inpatient admissions. Collaborate with the clinical team for initiation of remote monitoring services. Monitor and manage alerts, provide education and assess patient understanding for use. Act as a central point of contact for all patients, including interaction with medical, nursing, and ancillary services Develop and coordinate individual nursing plan-of-care including patient/family education and discharge planning. Drive to patients’ homes within Franklin and the six contiguous counties in a university-provided vehicle to provide in-home care. May support provider with patient identification and enrollment activities. Participate in ongoing improvement initiatives to foster a culture of high quality and patient safety Come join a team that is driving innovation and delivering high quality care to patients in their home! Organizational Expectations   Supports the nursing professional practice model. Practices within the Medical Center’s policies and procedures.  Adheres to OSUWMCs Values as demonstrated thought positive patient/guest relations, positive and effective interactions with staff, and formulating and meeting developmental goals. Minimum Qualifications For Hire:  Degree in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program required.  Current Ohio RN license or interim permit. Minimum of 2 years’ clinical experience in the acute care setting, preferably in a medical-surgical, progressive care environment or emergency department. *Experience in relevant care setting preferred. Valid United States or Canadian driver’s license. Ability to work independently, be self-directed and adapt to unpredictable circumstances. Effective interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills. Ability to problem-solve and iterate process improvements in delivery of home-based hospital level care Computer savvy and effectively utilizes technology, including Remote Patient Monitoring (RPM) to gather, report and analyze clinical data. On-going: Maintains current Ohio RN license and valid United States or Canadian driver’s license. Meets mandatory educational and health requirements.  Demonstrates competence in technical, interpersonal, and cognitive skills required to meet essential job functions. Job Relationships Supervisory Responsibility: N/A Contacts: Interacts with physician leaders, attending and resident staff, medical students, inpatient nursing, case management and social work staff, Medical Information Management staff, financial services and other members of the health care team, patients and families. Responsible to: Home & Post-Acute Operations Consultant, Hospital Care at Home Nursing Lead Physical/Visual/Mental Requirements The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  While performing the duties of this job, the employee must be able to: Transport/ move patients to provide care, Move objects weighing up to 40 pounds around the work environment to provide care (does not include patient movement or transfers) Provide care, perform necessary duties and maintain patient safety in the patient care environment, Set up/ adjust various patient equipment items, and Communicate clearly to facilitate the patient’s plan of care. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee is occasionally required to use hand to finger, handle or fell objects, tools or controls; and reach with hands or arms. Specific vision abilities required by the job include close vision, distance vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. Work Environment The work environment involves risks or discomforts which require special safety precautions, additional safety education and/or health risk monitoring, e.g. chemicals, radiation, working with sharps (needles, syringes, scalpels), infectious diseases.  Employees may be required to use protective clothing or gear such as masks, gowns, goggles, gloves, etc. The work environment involves everyday risks or discomforts which requires normal safety precautions typical of such places as offices and meeting rooms (i.e. use of safe work practices, avoidance of trips and falls, and observance of fire regulations and traffic signs). The work environment involves risks associated with the use of computers such as eye strain and disorders that result from repetitive motions associated with computer use. The work environment involves risks associated with operating motor vehicles such as vehicular accidents and hazardous road conditions (eg. Weather-related, night-driving, etc.). Additional Information: Thank you for your interest in this position. Due to program operations, onboarding is expected to begin in late October or early November. Location: Ackerman Rd, 660 (0242) Position Type: Intermittent Scheduled Hours: 0.2 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Health-System-Shared-Services/Home-Hospital-RN_R137799-1": {
      "title": "Home Hospital RN",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Home Hospital RN Department: Shared Services | Post-Acute and Home Based Care Services Hospital Care at Home is an innovative care model that allows us to provide inpatient level care to patients in their homes. Potential patients are assessed by a Home Hospital provider to ensure their diagnosis can be treated in the home, that the patient’s home environment is a safe place to receive care, and that the patient has consented to participate. We have successfully cared for more than 500 patients in Hospital Care at Home and are excited to continue to grow! The Home Hospital RN will partner closely with the attending physician and other members of the care team to provide care for patients, both virtually and through in-home visits. Primary responsibilities include: Participate in the initial and ongoing assessment of patients determining care and services needed to stay in the home. Collaborate with medical providers, patient care staff and skilled services in the planning and implementation of patient care plan. Direct and coordinate services (i.e., nursing, therapy, care management, etc.) provided in the home during the inpatient admissions. Collaborate with the clinical team for initiation of remote monitoring services. Monitor and manage alerts, provide education and assess patient understanding for use. Act as a central point of contact for all patients, including interaction with medical, nursing, and ancillary services Develop and coordinate individual nursing plan-of-care including patient/family education and discharge planning. Drive to patients’ homes within Franklin and the six contiguous counties in a university-provided vehicle to provide in-home care. May support provider with patient identification and enrollment activities. Participate in ongoing improvement initiatives to foster a culture of high quality and patient safety Come join a team that is driving innovation and delivering high quality care to patients in their home! Organizational Expectations   Supports the nursing professional practice model. Practices within the Medical Center’s policies and procedures.  Adheres to OSUWMCs Values as demonstrated thought positive patient/guest relations, positive and effective interactions with staff, and formulating and meeting developmental goals. Minimum Qualifications For Hire:  Degree in Nursing from a CCNE (Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education) or Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) accredited nursing program required.  Current Ohio RN license or interim permit. Minimum of 2 years’ clinical experience in the acute care setting, preferably in a medical-surgical, progressive care environment or emergency department. *Experience in relevant care setting preferred. Valid United States or Canadian driver’s license. Ability to work independently, be self-directed and adapt to unpredictable circumstances. Effective interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills. Ability to problem-solve and iterate process improvements in delivery of home-based hospital level care Computer savvy and effectively utilizes technology, including Remote Patient Monitoring (RPM) to gather, report and analyze clinical data. On-going: Maintains current Ohio RN license and valid United States or Canadian driver’s license. Meets mandatory educational and health requirements.  Demonstrates competence in technical, interpersonal, and cognitive skills required to meet essential job functions. Job Relationships Supervisory Responsibility: N/A Contacts: Interacts with physician leaders, attending and resident staff, medical students, inpatient nursing, case management and social work staff, Medical Information Management staff, financial services and other members of the health care team, patients and families. Responsible to: Home & Post-Acute Operations Consultant, Hospital Care at Home Nursing Lead Physical/Visual/Mental Requirements The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  While performing the duties of this job, the employee must be able to: Transport/ move patients to provide care, Move objects weighing up to 40 pounds around the work environment to provide care (does not include patient movement or transfers) Provide care, perform necessary duties and maintain patient safety in the patient care environment, Set up/ adjust various patient equipment items, and Communicate clearly to facilitate the patient’s plan of care. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee is occasionally required to use hand to finger, handle or fell objects, tools or controls; and reach with hands or arms. Specific vision abilities required by the job include close vision, distance vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. Work Environment The work environment involves risks or discomforts which require special safety precautions, additional safety education and/or health risk monitoring, e.g. chemicals, radiation, working with sharps (needles, syringes, scalpels), infectious diseases.  Employees may be required to use protective clothing or gear such as masks, gowns, goggles, gloves, etc. The work environment involves everyday risks or discomforts which requires normal safety precautions typical of such places as offices and meeting rooms (i.e. use of safe work practices, avoidance of trips and falls, and observance of fire regulations and traffic signs). The work environment involves risks associated with the use of computers such as eye strain and disorders that result from repetitive motions associated with computer use. The work environment involves risks associated with operating motor vehicles such as vehicular accidents and hazardous road conditions (eg. Weather-related, night-driving, etc.). Additional Information: Thank you for your interest in this position. Due to program operations, onboarding is expected to begin in late October or early November.  Location: Ackerman Rd, 660 (0242) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 36 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
