    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/James-Cancer-Hospital-and-Solove-Research-Institute/Clinical-Laboratory-Manager---Surgical-Pathology-Gross-Room_R155301-1": {
      "title": "Clinical Laboratory Manager - Surgical Pathology Gross Room",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Clinical Laboratory Manager - Surgical Pathology Gross Room Department: Medicine | Pathology OSUWMC Main Job Description Clinical Laboratory Manager who will serve as supervisor of the Surgical Pathology Gross Room (GR) Laboratory and Tissue Procurement Services (TPS) within the Anatomic Pathology Branch of the Department of Pathology. Responsibilities Manages and oversees the daily laboratory operations related to clinical and research activities including receipt of specimens, data entry into various information system applications, frozen section services, grossing of tissue and/or procurement of remnant tissue for research, coordination of technical work flow activities between histology and/or autopsy services, and communication with pathology physician leadership and research investigators related to technical management of surgical tissues; oversees and manages clinical and research staff including the hiring process; all technical training activities and requirements; competency assessment activities as required by regulatory guidelines; annual performance assessment; and when needed, employee disciplinary activities; manages and maintains a current GR and TPS standard operating policy and procedure manual; oversees and manages quality control and quality assurance activities pertaining to clinical and research tissue and related grossing or procurement for research; reports and discusses quality activities to the Anatomic pathology Technical Quality Improvement Committee; works in conjunction with other lab supervisors and faculty pathologists to ensure accurate and thorough operational compliance; investigates and manages issues of non-compliance including communication to pathology administrative and physician leadership; coordinates training and educational opportunities for medical students and residents; ensures prompt resolution of non-compliance and continuous process improvement; prepares and monitors annual GR finances and budget; ensures compliance with mandated safety requirements and regulations; provides grossing activities during periods of inadequate staff coverage; ensures operational compliance based on regulatory and accreditation standards; participates in short and long term strategic planning with regards to Gross Room and TPS operations; participates in special projects as assigned. Job Requirements Bachelors degree in Biological Sciences or equivalent education requirements. 5 years of relevant experience required. American Society of Clinical Pathology Certified in Pathologist Assistant. Additional Information: Clinical Laboratories / Surgical Pathology - People Leader - Managerial - M2 Manager Location: James Cancer Hospital (0375) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
