    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Research-Associate--Sustainable-Greenhouse-and-Nursery-Systems-Lab--Owens-Lab-_R157078-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate, Sustainable Greenhouse and Nursery Systems Lab (Owen Lab)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Research Associate, Sustainable Greenhouse and Nursery Systems Lab (Owen Lab) Department: FAES | Horticulture and Crop Science The Research Associate will work in the Sustainable Greenhouse and Nursery Systems lab (Owen Lab) located on Ohio State University Columbus campus. Greenhouse research support will be located in the Controlled Environment Agriculture Research Complex (CEARC) and Howlett Hall Greenhouses. Laboratory research assistance will occur in Howlett Hall and the CEARC Wet Lab. Work will include general greenhouse and tissue culture plant production and data collection, data analysis, writing and reporting, and administrative and programmatic support. Typical work duties of the selected candidate may include: Support the PD (Dr. Owen) in the design, management, and execution of greenhouse, nursery, tissue culture, and laboratory research projects. Greenhouse, nursery, and tissue culture tasks will include but not limited to scheduling seed sow, sticking unrooted cuttings, picking up nursery liners or plants; or creating media and maintaining tissue culture plants; pot or tray filling; transplanting; weekday and weekend watering and plant checks; crop maintenance including pest and disease pesticide applications; data collection and plant harvest; sanitation; and photographing plants and/or samples. Laboratory tasks will include equipment maintenance and logging; sample preparation, analysis, and shipping; and data collection, entry, analysis, visualization, and interpretation. Ordering supplies and reconciling requests. Scheduling product delivery. Analyze data sets using statistical software (SAS) or RStudio. Visualize data using SigmaPlot. Generate scientific and industry reports. Generate scientific peer-reviewed publications. Communicate research results at scientific and industry meetings and/or conferences. Train undergraduate research assistants to execute greenhouse, nursery, and laboratory tasks. Support research showcases, including preparation and clean up, when requested. Support would include planning, presenting, and communicating research results. Other duties will be assigned as needed to complete projects, reporting and writing responsibilities. Moderate physical exertion related to greenhouse and nursery activities such as lifting, pushing, pulling, and mixing of light to heavy objects; moving plants; standing for long periods of time; and exposure to heat, light, and wet greenhouse conditions will occur. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or equivalent experience in a greenhouse and laboratory required; 4 years of relevant experience required with High School diploma or GED, 2 years of relevant experience required with Associate's Degree, or 0 years of relevant experience required with Bachelor's Degree. Proficient with Microsoft Excel, Microsoft PowerPoint, Microsoft Word, statistical software (SAS or RStudio), Sigma Plot, and Camtasia (or equivalent video editing program). Excellent oral and written communication skills required. Scientific writing skills and experience required. Excellent organizational skills and personal management. Preferred Qualifications: Master's of Science degree  and Greenhouse and/or controlled environment production experience preferred.  Additional Information: This job profile is a Research Technician 3 (T3 level) on the career roadmap. The offer for this position will fall within the positions pay range based on internal equity, unit’s available budget, and the candidate’s qualifications Location: Howlett Hall (0295) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Stu-Learn-to-Swim-Instructor-Non-OSU_R157440": {
      "title": "Stu Learn to Swim Instructor-Non-OSU",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Stu Learn to Swim Instructor-Non-OSU Department: Student Life | Recreational Sports Administration-JM Job Summary:     Learn to Swim Instructors at the McCorkle Aquatic Pavilion and RPAC Recreation Natatorium are a select team of individuals that teach swimming lessons for participants 6-months through adults. Instructors teach skills in a logical progression, allowing participants to learn to swim and play safely in and around the water.      Classes are held during the academic year on Sundays 1 0 :30 am -5:00pm for group lessons and Sunday through Friday for private lessons. The Learn-to-Swim Program provides an increased emphasis in the areas of drowning prevention and water safety and an all-encompassing approach to swimming and water safety through the American Red Cross. Instructors may teach both Group and Private Lessons.     This position provides the opportunity to develop life and professional skills such as time management, responsibility attention to detail, adaptability , communication, and learning to work under pressure. Staff have the opportunity to work with groups and individuals of various ages.     This p osition is i deal for someone who is looking for a flexible, rewarding, and FUN job on campus! We do not have lessons on Saturdays in the Fall and are off during school breaks and holidays!     Requirements:   Experience in teaching group and/or private swimming lessons.    Complete the new hire evaluation .   Regularly attend and participate in meetings, in-service trainings , and skills checks.     Responsibilities:   Responsible for the safety and care of students during specified class times.   Ensure adherence to American Red Cross Instructor guidelines .   Demonstrate a comprehensive knowledge of, and comply with, the facility rules, and policies and procedures, and consistently and appropriately enforce them as outlined in the Aquatic Staff Manual.   D evelop safe , progressional, and age-appropriate lessons for group and private classes.   Prepare individual lesson plans and collaborate and plan with co-instructor s when assigned shared classes .    M anag e participant behavior in accordance with program guidelines.   Complete administrative duties such as submitting program paperwork in a timely manner and maintaining attendance sheets.   C ommunicate with swim parents (or adult participants) to provide feedback about swimmer progress .   A ssist with strategic planning for the program and attend regular staff training sessions and meetings.   Consistently project a positive, professional image and always provide consistent high quality customer service.   Keep up to date with staff correspondence and updates.   Consistently demonstrate positive, effective communication skills.   Perform other duties and tasks as assigned.     Availability Requirements:   Provide a schedule of availability to the scheduling supervisor as requested – staff will be scheduled shifts around academic commitments.   Ability to regularly work Sundays 1 0 :30 am -5:00pm .   Ability to regularly work one or more weekday evenings 4-8 p.m. for private lessons.   Ability to teach a minimum of 2 hours of private lessons a week.       Pay Rate:   $ 1 3 . 65 per hour (non-WSI)   $14.00 per hour (WSI Certified)   Merit increases may be available after semester of work.     Additional Information :    Please list your contact information in a resume.   A fingerprint background check – provided by OSU – is required for all positions working with minors on campus and will occur during the screening process .     American Red Cross CPR /AED-PR and First Aid certification is required within 90 days of hire – certification , if needed, is provided by OSU at no cost to you.   Employees will be required to participate in paid mandatory training at the start of and throughout their employment with Recreational Sports .     Staff will have the opportunity to participate in a FREE American Red Cross Water Safety Instructor ( WSI ) class once hired if they desire to obtain that certification. Along with the certification, the staff’s pay will be increased to $14.00.     Additional Job Description :   Mission : The Office of Student Life fosters students' development, learning, well-being and sense of belonging; empowers students to achieve their academic, personal and professional goals; and prepares students to be engaged in a global society.     Area Statement: Individuals working in aquatics receive specialized training related to health and safety to meet the legal requirements outlined in the State of Ohio Pool and Spa Code. They maintain a high level of responsibility and are required to exercise sound judgement in the completion of their duties. Strong swimming skills are required for all positions.   Additional Information: Location: McCorkle Aquatic Pavilion (0247) Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 5 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/College-of-MedicineOffice-of-Health-Sciences/Researcher-3-Medical-Oncology_R154436-1": {
      "title": "Researcher 3-Medical Oncology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Researcher 3-Medical Oncology Department: Medicine | IM Medical Oncology Researcher responsible for performing experiments and managing projects in a clinical/translational lung cancer research lab. Planned projects are translationally important from clinical perspective and will employ cutting edge laboratory and analytical techniques. This role will focus on tumor signaling and interactions with the immune microenvironment in lung tumors that have loss of the LKB1 tumor suppressor, with goals of gaining mechanistic insight into the important clinical question of why these tumors are resistant to immunotherapy treatments, and identification and testing of candidate pathways that could be targeted to enhance immune sensitivity. Using in vitro (tumor cell lines, and a T-cell co-culture system) and in vivo model systems (murine cell lines from an LKB1 deficient GEMM that can be used for immunocompetent allograft experiments, as well as the GEMM model itself), to test hypotheses on pathways responsible for immune resistance. Conduct cutting edge high throughput experiments with functional genomics screens (e.g. CRISPRi based screens), proteomics and phosphoproteomics, single cell RNAseq, to help dissect out the mechanisms that may be responsible for these effects, which can both strengthen conclusions from hypothesis based mechanistic studies, and also can be used to gain novel insights and identify new hypotheses. Results from preclinical work will be integrated with analyses from existing multi-omic data, and also access to clinical trial specimens and/or OSU clinical cohorts to test ideas in specimens from lung cancer patients. MINIMUM REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Master's Degree in Biological Sciences or relevant field, or equivalent experience required; 5 years of relevant experience required with Bachelor's Degree, or 3 years of relevant experience required with Master's Degree. A background in cancer biology and/or immunology is a plus. Function: Research and Scholarship Sub Function: Research Career Band: Individual Contributor – Specialized Career Level: S3 Additional Information: The Ohio State University is a dynamic community of diverse resources, where opportunity thrives and where individuals transform themselves and the world. The Ohio State University is one of the nation’s largest and most comprehensive public universities and a top employer in Ohio. As one of only 57 designated comprehensive cancer centers in the nation, The Ohio State University Comprehensive Cancer Center – Arthur G. James Cancer Hospital and Richard J. Solove Research Institute is dedicated to the creation of knowledge in laboratory, clinical and population-based cancer research. We apply those discoveries to develop more effective approaches to cancer prevention, diagnosis, and therapies – providing tomorrow’s standard of care today. A Cancer-Free World Begins Here. The OSUCCC – James is the only cancer program in the United States that features a National Cancer Institute (NCI)-designated comprehensive cancer center aligned with a nationally ranked academic medical center and a freestanding cancer hospital on the campus of one of the nation’s largest public universities. is the only cancer program in the United States that features a National Cancer Institute (NCI)-designated comprehensive cancer center aligned with a nationally ranked academic medical center and a freestanding cancer hospital on the campus of one of the nation’s largest public universities. Location: Biomedical Research Tower (0112) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
