    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Health-System-Shared-Services/Manager--Building-Automation-Systems_R156409-1": {
      "title": "Manager, Building Automation Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Manager, Building Automation Systems Department: James | CCCT James Facility Services Scope of Position The Ohio State Medical Center is committed to enhancing the quality of care provided to patients. The Supervisor, Facilities Operations functions to support the Medical Center's day-to-day operations with functional and financial management of associates assigned to building operations and maintenance. Position Summary The Supervisor, Facilities Operations is responsible for all managerial functions for designated facilities operations employees. This includes associates from the Mechanical Systems, Electric and Electronic Systems, and Building Systems shops. This position is responsible for the day-to-day operations, maintenance, repairs and projects of the Medical Center facilities. This includes, but is not limited to electric, plumbing, medical gas, beds, fire alarms, material handling system, HVAC/R and general repair and upkeep of the building environment and life safety compartments. This position encompasses communication, coordination, and regulatory compliance for all assigned areas. This position is responsible for the supervision of all assigned personnel and for the operations and regulatory compliance of the assigned areas, designated systems, and equipment. The position is responsible for inspecting, assessing, coordinating, delegating and evaluating personnel performance and will prioritize personnel and shop activities related to the maintaining of the facilities grounds and buildings. Areas and equipment are operated 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. May cover for other supervisors due to absence and vacation, as necessary. The supervisor is subject to call back. Responsibilities include actively promoting the Medical Center’s mission, vision and values in support of an absolute customer satisfaction. Minimum Qualifications For Hire: Bachelor’s degree in related field or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Three (3) years progressive supervisory experience required. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Additional Information: Location: Ackerman Rd, 650 (0241) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
