    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Assistant-Vice-Provost-for-University-Admissions_R155907": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice Provost for University Admissions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Assistant Vice Provost for University Admissions Department: Strategic Enrollment | Strategic Enrollment Administration The Opportunity   The Assistant Vice Provost for University Admissions serves as a key member of the Strategic Enrollment Management (SEM) senior leadership team and reports directly to the Vice Provost for Strategic Enrollment Management. This leadership role provides vision, strategy, and operational oversight for the university's admissions enterprise, including undergraduate admissions, graduate and professional admissions, admissions systems and imaging, and recruitment and enrollment initiatives for Ohio State's regional campuses.   The Assistant Vice Provost is responsible for advancing the university's enrollment goals through the development and execution of comprehensive admissions and recruitment strategies aligned with institutional priorities and the SEM strategic plan. The role leads the establishment of strategic goals, policies, processes, budgets, and performance measures that support student access, enrollment growth, operational excellence, and student success.   As the university's senior admissions leader, the Assistant Vice Provost directs the operations of Undergraduate Admissions, providing strategic leadership for domestic and international enrollment initiatives, enrollment planning, and the continuous enhancement of admissions technologies and processes. The position champions a culture of accountability and performance excellence while ensuring compliance with institutional, state, and federal regulations, mitigating risk, and overseeing admissions appeals and policy matters.   In partnership with Enrollment Analytics, Student Financial Aid, Marketing and Strategic Communications, and academic leadership across the university, the Assistant Vice Provost leverages data-driven insights to inform recruitment, admission, and enrollment strategies. The role oversees the implementation of integrated marketing and communications plans that strengthen student recruitment efforts and support enrollment objectives across the Columbus campus, regional campuses, and Ohio State ATI. The Assistant Vice Provost provides strategic counsel and operational leadership to advance institutional enrollment priorities. The position fosters transparency, collaboration, and alignment across undergraduate and graduate academic units and colleges, while strengthening pathways to Ohio State through pipeline programs, transfer initiatives, community partnerships, and student transition programs that expand access and opportunity.   The Assistant Vice Provost represents the university through service on institutional, regional, and national committees, task forces, and professional organizations, serving as a prominent advocate for Ohio State and its enrollment mission. Through visionary leadership and cross-campus collaboration, this role plays a critical part in shaping the university's enrollment strategy and ensuring continued success in attracting, enrolling, and supporting a talented student population. Bachelor's degree required, 10+ years progressive leadership experience required. Advanced degree and experience in an academic setting preferred. Additional Information: How to Apply Inquiries, nominations and applications are invited. For full consideration, applicant materials should be received by September 28, 2026. Applicants should submit the following : Letter of Interest: Include a 1–2-page summary of your background and why you are interested in this opportunity. Resume: Detailed overview of your experience. Location: Student Academic Services (0160) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Assistant-Teacher-1_R156904-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Teacher 1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Assistant Teacher 1 Department: Human Resources | Child Care Program Position Overview: The Assistant Teacher assists in supervising and integrating all daily and long-term planning for the classroom in collaboration with the support team and other classroom team members. Our assistant teachers ensure that the social, emotional, physical, and educational needs of the children are met based on the center's philosophy, curriculum, policies, and state licensing rules. They consistently implement, evaluate, and communicate classroom programming, routines, and procedures. Additionally, they are required to manage the classroom by completing the necessary paperwork, training, evaluating staff, and problem-solving with the team and parents. Our assistant teachers implement health, safety, and security processes and procedures, including CACFP meal counting. Furthermore, they participate in professional development and center-wide and university teams, as well as individually planned activities. Department Overview: The Child Care Program is licensed by the State of Ohio Department of Jobs and Family Services and is accredited by the National Association for the Education of Young Children (NAEYC). This prestigious recognition has been achieved by less than 10% of early childhood programs nationwide. The NAEYC accreditation is a rigorous, voluntary process by which early childhood programs demonstrate that they meet national standards of excellence. Required Qualifications: High School Diploma The Child Care Program at Ackerman Rd is offering a new hire bonus of $1000. $500 after 6 months of continued employment and another $500 payment after one year of continued employment with the Child Care Center at The Ohio State University! To learn more about the Child Care Program, please visit our website . Additional Information: Location: Child Care Center (0385) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
