    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Wooster-Campus/Assistant-Professor_R151805": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. You will be presented with the opportunity to attach up to five (5) documents in the Application Documents section. If necessary, please consider combining documents into one file. If you require any assistance with including the necessary documents in the application process, please reach out to HRConnection@osu.edu . Resume parsing is not effective on documents which exceed one (1) page.  As a result, it is not recommended to select Autofill with Resume when applying if using a resume or CV which exceeds one (1) page. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Assistant Professor Department: FAES | Horticulture and Crop Science Tenure faculty (regardless of rank) - persons with the titles of professor, associate professor, assistant professor and instructor who serve on appointments totaling 50% or more service to the university and who are eligible for tenure or who have obtained tenure. Duties and responsibilities are assigned in accordance with the workload guidelines laid out in the pattern of administration of each faculty member’s tenure initiation unit (TIU) and, as appropriate, regional campus; obligations will include research, service and/or teaching or clinical practice.  These faculty will have earned doctorate or other terminal degree in the relevant field of study or possession of equivalent experience. Additional Information: Assistant Professor in The Ohio State University, Department of Horticulture and Crop Science, College of Food, Agricultural, and Environmental Sciences, Wooster, Ohio.    Duties: teach undergraduate and graduate courses in horticulture, crop science, vegetable production, and related topics; research concerning horticultural food production systems with a focus on urban and urbanizing environments and communities; support university extension efforts through collaboration with community stakeholders; service to university, college, and profession.   Requirements:  Ph.D. in Agronomy and Horticulture, Crop Science, Plant Science, Soil Science, Sustainable Agriculture, Agroecology, or related field; potential in applied research as demonstrated by publications, presentations, or dissertation in agriculture, crop science, soil science, or related subjects; requires successful completion of a background check.   EOE/AA/M/F/Vet/Disability Employer. Location: Williams Hall (0414) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: The Ohio State University believes in diversity in people and ideas. What Ohio State does matters. And how we do it matters. When we are at our best, we make a real difference to people. Our size, breadth, geography, history and standard of excellence position us to drive the future of higher education. We believe that the university should be a place where people can work and learn together in a safe environment, free of violence, harassment, discrimination, exploitation, or intimidation. As such, finalists for any faculty position that carries tenure must sign an authorization and disclosure form, which will allow current or prior employer(s) to share information to the University regarding any findings of employment-related misconduct or disciplinary proceedings against a candidate and/or any pending investigations related to alleged misconduct. Such information shall include findings and pending investigations with respect to sexual harassment, violence, or harassment; research misconduct; financial fraud or misconduct; foreign influence violations, grant misuse or misconduct; and/or any other type of finding or pending investigation relating to a candidate’s employer’s policies and rules governing faculty conduct that may reasonably be expected to affect a candidate’s appointment. If the University becomes aware of any past finding of misconduct or pending investigations that were not disclosed, Ohio State will treat that as a serious omission and reserves the right to rescind an offer or terminate employment. Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Manager--Financial-Operations---Pathology_R154069-1": {
      "title": "Manager, Financial Operations - Pathology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Manager, Financial Operations - Pathology Department: Medicine | Pathology Position Summary Finance Manager to direct, lead and manage all fiscal affairs for Department of Pathology within College of Medicine(COM), and its clinical practice plan through The Ohio State University Physicians (OSUP) and the Ohio State University Faculty Group Practice (FGP).  Under the direction of the Department Administrator directs and preserves established financial and operational processing environment; ensures adherence to appropriate internal control structures and compliance with established fiscal policies, procedures, regulations and updates as appropriate; participates on executive team in overall management of department and may serve as Department Administrator in his/her absence; participates in short-term and long-term strategic planning activities for department and clinical practice group; develops and implements long-term financial plans and objectives; develops, implements and administers annual budgets including academic, earnings  and practice plan  budgets; oversees and controls departmental funds including operating, endowment, development, salary recovery and research start-up funds; manages and oversees all contracts and agreements, billing and accounts receivable, and accounting activities administration; develops, implements and administers annual budgets; develops, implements and periodically evaluates department fiscal policies and procedures; advises Department Administrator, Department Chair, and Board of Managers of private practice group on strategic and operational financial matters; gathers data and prepares financial reports including Sources and Uses across missions  to include research, endowments and development funds; analyzes, interprets and prepares required OSUP/FGP fiscal reports; presents financial reports and performance indicators to department and clinical practice group leadership and members; recruits, hires and trains fiscal support staff; supervises and evaluates staff; reports to Chief Administrative Officer of Pathology Job Duties Breakdown 40% - Directs, leads and manages all fiscal affairs for the Department of Pathology and its clinical practice plan under the direction of the Department Administrator; directs and preserves established financial and operational processing environment; ensures adherence to appropriate internal control structures and compliance with established fiscal policies, procedures and regulations; develops and implements long term financial plans and objectives; develops, implements and periodically evaluates department fiscal policies and procedures; advises Department Administrator, Chair, and Board of Managers of the practice group on strategic and operational financial matters; oversees planning and preparation for and participates in internal and external audits; serves as fiscal liaison to the COM and OSUP/FGP. 25% - Develops, implements and administers annual budgets including earnings and academic and practice plan budgets; oversees and controls departmental funds including operating, endowment, development, salary recovery and research start-up funds; manages and oversees all contracts and agreements, billing and accounts receivable, and accounting activities and administration; reviews and authorizes all expenditures, journal entries, income and transfers; analyzes, interprets and reconciles financial reports; identifies discrepancies and determines resolution; reviews pathology research funds and provides financial analysis of potential or actual project overruns; develops and presents quarterly financial reports to department leadership and board of clinical practice group managers; serves as liaison with OSUP/FGP central business office for departmental patient accounts receivables (AR) including main AR, OSU Histology Lab LLC; initiates OSUPS monthly invoices for Part A and URL Part B; oversees preparation of OSUPS contract income and patient revenue budget; prepares OSUPS budgets 20% - Oversees and manages faculty compensation including base salaries, incentives, research bonuses, annual merit compensation and supplemental compensation;  prepares annual faculty salary budget within rank showing sources of funding for Department Chairman review; collaborates with Department Chair and Administrator to determine faculty compensation and salary adjustments; reviews, determines and prepares release time calculations; develops, prepares and monitors research metrics for review by department chair and vice chair of experimental research; prepares faculty productivity model for Department Chairman review; monitors and reviews clinical faculty logging records. 15% - Participates in overall management of department, may serve as Department Administrator in his/her absence; participates in short and long term strategic planning activities for department and clinical practice group; participates in and provides financial recommendation with pathology outreach program initiatives; oversees  management of  OSU Pathology Services (OSUPS) payables and receivables; approves OSUPS cash and investment transfers; oversees financial performance of the OSU Histology Lab LLC; other duties as assigned. Job Requirements Bachelor's Degree in Accounting, Business Administration, or related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience is required; Master's Degree preferred; 5 years relevant experience required, 8-12 years of relevant experience preferred. Additional Information: Finance / Financial Operations - People Leader - Managerial - M2 Manager Location: Optometry Clinic (1041) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Outpatient-CareAmbulatory/Sr-Supply-Chain-Coordinator_R152623-1": {
      "title": "Sr Supply Chain Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Sr Supply Chain Coordinator Department: Ambulatory Services | 161 and Hamilton Administration Job Description Under the supervision of the Supply Chain Manager or Assistant Director, coordinates and administers a lean supply support system designed to operate efficiently and meet the needs of clinical areas across OSU Wexner Medical Center. Maintains and manages inventory levels within assigned clinical areas and performs a full range of supply chain functions in procedural areas, including demand forecasting, requisitioning, inventory control, and implant/consignment management. Oversees case picking activities and collaborates with clinical staff to ensure the accuracy and maintenance of preference cards. Responsible for the implementation, monitoring, and ongoing maintenance of the two-bin Kanban inventory system. Serves as a key liaison among clinical staff, supply chain personnel, and vendors to address supply chain-related matters, including expiration date monitoring, cycle counting, annual physical inventories, par level analysis, product evaluations and trials, product conversions and discontinuations, preference card management, storage flow optimization, and overall supply room organization and efficiency. Minimum Qualifications High School diploma or GED and 2 years of inventory management experience. Additional Information: Our Comprehensive Employee Benefits Include: An array of retirement plan options, each with a generous employer contribution. Affordable health insurance options, including dental, vision and prescription coverage that begin on day one. Paid vacation and sick leave, including short and long-term disability and paid parental leave. Get the most out of the Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. And much more! Location: Ohio State Outpatient Care New Albany (1027) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/James-Cancer-Hospital-and-Solove-Research-Institute/Pharmacy-Technician---Outpatient_R156525-1": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Technician - Outpatient",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Pharmacy Technician - Outpatient Department: Retail Rx | OSU Outpatient Pharmacy Doan Scope of Position Responsible for supporting the safe, efficient, and compliant preparation and distribution of medications under the supervision of a licensed pharmacist. Provides high-quality, patient-centered technical support services to ensure accurate medication preparation, packaging, and inventory control. In collaboration with pharmacists and other pharmacy technicians, assist in maintaining regulatory compliance, operational efficiency, and service excellence across assigned practice areas. Maintains active registration as a Pharmacy Technician Trainee or Registered Pharmacy Technician with the Ohio Board of Pharmacy and fulfills all continuing education and competency requirements necessary to maintain registration throughout employment. If registered as an Ohio Board of Pharmacy Technician Trainee, completion of the OSUWMC employer-based training program is required within 365 days of hire, followed by updating registration to Registered Pharmacy Technician status with the Ohio Board of Pharmacy. Demonstrates professional conduct aligned with hospital and departmental mission, vision, and values. Position Summary This position functions to support all aspects of medication preparation and distribution services at The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center under the supervision of a licensed pharmacist. Duties include medication preparation and packaging; sterile and non-sterile compounding; inventory management; documentation; maintenance of medication storage and security standards; and other duties as permitted by Ohio Board of Pharmacy. The Pharmacy Technician I assists pharmacists in ensuring accurate medication dispensing and regulatory compliance in accordance with Ohio Board of Pharmacy rules, state and federal regulations, USP standards as applicable, and institutional policies. This role supports both patient care and research protocols while promoting a safe and efficient medication-use system. Must demonstrate knowledge and skills necessary to provide services appropriate to the age of the patients served, including completing any mandatory education requirements. Minimum Qualifications For Hire: High school diploma or equivalent. Minimum age: 18 years. Registered or eligible for pharmacy technician registration in Ohio. Pharmacy Technician Trainees must submit all required documentation to the Ohio Board of Pharmacy at least 10 business days before start date. Ongoing: Maintain Registered Pharmacy Technician status with Ohio Board of Pharmacy. Pharmacy Technician Trainees must obtain Registered Pharmacy Technician status within 1.5 years of hire. Continues to meet departmental competency requirements and pharmacy standards of employee conduct. Additional Information: The university will not sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. https://wexnermedical.osu.edu/pharmacy Location: James Cancer Hospital (0375) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/College-of-MedicineOffice-of-Health-Sciences/Morgue-Attendant---Pathology_R155776-1": {
      "title": "Morgue Attendant - Pathology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Morgue Attendant - Pathology Department: Medicine | Pathology Position Summary Under general supervision, functions as a Morgue Attendant providing periodic coverage of the Morgue (during business hours, after business hours, and holidays) managing routine receipt and release of decedents and routine phone coverage; processes funeral home notifications/designations, autopsy requests, organ procurement notifications, and coroner’s office referrals for each decedent, as applicable; assists with the transfer of decedents from cart/bed to cart/bed; completes documentation required for receipt/release protocols; performs data entry into databases including Microsoft Excel and SharePoint systems; guides transporters in proper receipt/release protocols; operates badge-only access points during after-hours coverage; communicates with clinical staff, non-OSU entities, residents, faculty, autopsy staff and more via email and fax regarding decedent updates, required documentation, hand-off notices, and other pertinent information; serves as a liaison with internal and external physicians, staff, researchers, families, funeral homes and representatives from other healthcare facilities Disposes of biohazardous and chemical waste safely and appropriately; requests pickup and delivery of environmental health and safety supplies; discards surgical and autopsy specimens, organizes and catalogs surgical specimens following transport from appropriate laboratories, delivers specimens and cassettes to appropriate laboratories; performs barcode scanning to track assets throughout workflows; prepares and closes conferences (cleans surfaces/tools/supplies, processes/replaces tissues) Reviews and obtains documentation associated with authorization from legal next-of-kin for autopsy; discusses autopsy authorization processes and requirements with families and non-OSU facility representatives; obtains medical records and documentation from internal and external sources; operates clinical and pathology-specific laboratory information systems to prepare autopsy cases; accessions cases to chart autopsy data/documents and produce case labels; prepares case folders including requesting/receiving, sorting, & entering autopsy data into laboratory information systems Performs routine and unanticipated cleaning; attends intra and interdivisional meetings; completes additional duties as assigned Job Requirements H igh School diploma or GED. Certification or vocational training may be preferred. 1 year of relevant experience required. 2-4 years of relevant experience preferred. Experience with the principles, operations and maintenance of laboratory procedures and equipment desired; ability to move a minimum of 100 pounds and lift a minimum of 50 pounds required; ability to conduct professional and empathetic phone conversations strongly desired; basic familiarity with medical terminology desired; computer skills including knowledge of basic internet operation and Microsoft Office required. Additional Information: Eligible for premium pay for shifts of at least four consecutive hours worked after 3:00 PM on weekdays, weekends, or holidays. Participation in an on-call rotation and occasional holiday coverage is required. Location: Davis Heart and Lung Research Institute (0113) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-Hospital/Administrative-Nursing-Supervisor_R154618-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Nursing Supervisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Administrative Nursing Supervisor Department: University Hospital | Clinical Resources Job Description Scope of Position The Administrative Nurse Supervisor (ANS) is responsible for administering clinical operations within The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center in partnership with nursing and physician leadership, administrator on-call (AOC) and leadership of the hospital. The Administrative Nurse Supervisor is responsible for enforcing hospital and nursing quality in collaboration with the Director of Nursing Quality, and hospital policies and procedures and supporting the professional practice of nursing. They are responsible to ensure that patients have adequate care by managing nurse schedules and interacting with healthcare professionals, patients, and visitors. The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center is committed to enhancing the quality of care our patients receive. Position Summary The Administrative Nurse Supervisor functions as an extension of the leadership team of The Ohio State University Wexner Medical Center, supervising the immediate care of our patients on a given shift, which includes making rounds to all patient care areas. To ensure care that is safe, effective, and efficient, the ANS obtains report from the charge nurse(s) and Nurse Manager and is knowledgeable of current patient(s) status. Administrative Nurse Supervisors facilitate communication between nurses and other disciplines, making sure that clear, organized processes are in place for informing staff members across work shifts. Assist with supervision of the staff on the nursing unit while on duty and contributes to evaluation of nursing and clinical ancillary staff, recommends performance action to the appropriate nurse manager including disciplinary actions and/or terminations. Coordinates nursing activities with those of related clinical departments and provides information for staffing needs. Functions as the representative for crisis, emergency, or unusual situations in collaboration with legal and administration. Complies and operates under the guidance of the Ohio Board of Nursing and other regulatory compliance and accreditation bodies. Promotes the practice of nursing, a just culture, focusing on safety, quality, and evidence-based practice. Manages risks to the organization in alignment with physicians and leadership. Maintains a strong focus on patient experience and staff engagement. Functions as a communication pathway for the Nursing Directors, Chief Nursing Officer, and other organizational leaders. Minimum Qualifications Graduate of an accredited school of nursing. Current Ohio licensure. Three years progressive hospital nursing experience is required and preferred in administration and supervision. BSN required. ACLS certification preferred/required after hire. Clinical certification preferred. Strong clinical experience. Strong skills related to effective communication, conflict management, decision-making, critical thinking, and time management Additional Information: Location: University Hospital - Doan Hall (0089) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: Rotating Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Post-Doctoral-Scholar---Biomedical-Informatics_R143686-1": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Scholar - Biomedical Informatics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Post Doctoral Scholar - Biomedical Informatics Department: Medicine | School Biomed Sci - Biomedical Informatics Post Doctoral Researcher to pursue specialized research training and experience under the guidance of a scientific mentor in the Department of Biomedical Informatics; designs and develops novel computational tools for biomedical data analysis; performs large-scale analysis using omics data; assists in identifying new biomedical data analysis technology and trends;  participates as a team member with lab staff, collaborative researchers, and students and to interpret data and discuss project progress; collaborates with other researchers in determining research priorities and planning programs of research; performs relevant published literature searches; assists with writing and submitting grant proposals to obtain extramural funding agencies; writes and prepares research manuscripts, articles, abstracts, and project reports; presents ongoing work and findings at local, national, and international conferences. Requirements Ph.D. degree in one of the following areas: Computer Science, Computer Science and Technology, or other disciplines with strong quantitative background. Proficiency in at least one programming language, such as R, C, Python or MATLAB, is strongly preferred; knowledge in genomics, genetics, or proteomics is desired but not required. Additional Information: Location: Lincoln Tower (0271) Position Type: Term (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
