    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Capital-Pillar-Senior-Analyst_R150777-1": {
      "title": "Senior Analyst, Innovation Investment Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Senior Analyst, Innovation Investment Management Department: ERIK | Technology Commercialization Position Summary The Ohio State University's Innovation Investment Management team sits within the Innovation and Commercialization function, where university research, technology commercialization, startup formation, venture capital, and portfolio stewardship intersect. As Ohio State technologies move toward licensing, startup creation, external funding, and market growth, the team manages the investment, fund reporting and portfolio activity connected to university innovation. The Senior Analyst, Innovation Investment Management, is a key member of the team supporting investment analysis, portfolio reporting, fund and external capital analysis, diligence materials, venture market intelligence, and portfolio research. This role is designed for an analytically strong candidate interested in working at the intersection of venture capital, startup finance, university innovation, fund investing, portfolio management, and technology commercialization. The Senior Analyst will support evaluation of startup, follow-on investment, fund, and external capital opportunities; prepare financial, market, ownership, fund, and portfolio analyses; monitor portfolio activity and fund performance; develop dashboards and committee materials; and translate data, documents, and market activity into decision-support materials for senior team members and leadership.  This role provides broad exposure to university-affiliated startups, early-stage investment activity, fund opportunities, external capital relationships, and innovation portfolio management, with a focus on analysis, reporting synthesis, diligence support, and venture market intelligence. Key Responsibilities Conduct due diligence and investment analysis for direct and follow-on investment opportunities involving university-affiliated startups and existing portfolio companies, as well as fund and external capital platform opportunities. Review fund reports, manager updates, capital activity, valuation changes, distributions, unfunded exposure, portfolio developments, and prospective fund materials; prepare summaries, dashboards, diligence support, and briefing materials for senior team members, committees, and leadership. Build financial analyses, market research, ownership analyses, fund summaries, exposure analyses, dashboards, and written materials that support investment decisions, participation rights evaluations, fund diligence, external capital discussions, and emerging capital deployment activity. Monitor portfolio performance, financing activity, milestone achievement, external capital raised, valuation changes, capital needs, and other indicators that inform portfolio reporting, impact assessment, and leadership decision-making.  Prepare portfolio reports, impact assessments, dashboards, briefing materials and presentations for leadership, investment and advisory committee meetings. Translate venture capital, fund investing, startup financing, university innovation, and commercialization trends into insights that support portfolio strategy and the development of Ohio State’s innovation investment platform.  Map funds, investors, sectors, markets, and external capital models, external capital models, and university-affiliated investment approaches to identify funding trends, market dynamics, portfolio capital needs, and areas of alignment with Ohio State-affiliated startups, portfolio priorities, and fund investment strategy. Maintain investment analysis files, portfolio research, diligence materials, fund reporting inputs, and supporting documentation used for internal decision-making, in coordination with other IIM team members. Coordinate with founders, faculty, commercialization teams, portfolio companies, fund managers, and internal stakeholders to gather information, support diligence and reporting needs, and maintain visibility into investment and portfolio activity.   Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in business, finance, economics, public administration, or related field. 4 years of relevant experience required in investment analysis, economic development, venture capital, or related areas. Demonstrated strong quantitative, analytical, and financial modeling skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. High attention to detail, organization, and deadline management. Experience with Excel, PowerPoint, and data/portfolio management platforms. Desired Qualifications Advanced degree (MBA, Master’s, or related area). 4-8 years of relevant experience. Experience supporting investment analysis, venture capital, startup finance, fund investing, university commercialization, innovation investment, economic development, or portfolio management activities within a university, public sector, venture, finance or technology/startup ecosystem. Familiarity with commercialization pathways, early-stage venture investing, fund investing, cap tables, ownership analysis, fund performance metrics, impact assessment, and portfolio reporting. Experience with PitchBook, Carta, Chronograph, Excel dashboards, Power BI, Tableau, Smartsheet, SharePoint, or similar research, reporting, or portfolio systems. Application Materials A resume is required. A cover letter is desired. Additional Information: Salary The salary range for this job profile is $88,300 - $115,350 . The offer for this position may fall within this range based on multiple factors including internal equity, unit’s available budget, and the candidate’s qualifications. Additional Information: Due to U.S. export control regulations governing information, technology, and facilities accessed during the performance of work, applicants must be: (1) U.S. citizens or nationals; (2) permanent residents; (3) asylees or refugees; or (4) individuals otherwise described as “protected individuals” pursuant to Title 8 U.S. Code Section 1324b(a)(3)(b). Ohio State will not sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. ERIK Overview Join the Enterprise for Research, Innovation and Knowledge (ERIK) at The Ohio State University and become a part of a dynamic, forward-thinking team dedicated to pushing the boundaries of discovery and innovation. ERIK positions Ohio State to expand curiosity-driven research and creative expression, further develop our research community of faculty, staff, and students, and grow the innovation ecosystem to address big challenges and improve communities locally and globally. We are seeking passionate individuals who are committed to making a meaningful impact through collaboration, innovation, and excellence. To learn more about our mission and work, please visit https://erik.osu.edu/ . Location: Energy Advancement and Innovation Center (1044) Position Type: Regular Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Harding-Hospital/Social-Worker---IRP-2_R148658-1": {
      "title": "Social Worker - Contingent",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Social Worker - Contingent Department: Harding | Harding Social Work SCOPE OF POSITION The Wexner Medical Center at Ohio State University and Harding Hospital are committed to enhancing the quality of care that our patients receive. The Inpatient Social Worker: Psychiatric functions within the Interdisciplinary Treatment Team to provide patient care and supportive services that are directed at achievement of patient care outcomes, maximizing the patients involvement in his/her own care plan, improving service levels, reducing the length of hospitalization, and decreasing costs. Patients and their family will experience the benefits of patient focused care through the integrated skills of all treatment team members. Services provided include 24-hour crisis care, 24-hour inpatient care, outpatient services, ECT, TMS, and partial hospitalization for psychiatric patients. Inpatient Psychiatric Social Worker services include psychosocial assessment, treatment planning, counseling, crisis intervention, and patient/family education. Social workers work within the Interdisciplinary Treatment Team to provide these supportive functions, and also may assist with discharge planning to facilitate the transition from hospital treatment to continuing mental health care following inpatient treatment. Inpatient Psychiatric Social Workers manage their own caseload of patients and provide social work services to patient and/or families who receive inpatient psychiatric treatment. Wexner Medical Center at The Ohio State University and OSU Harding Hospital are committed to providing world class patient care by Interdisciplinary Treatment Teams. Psychiatric Social Workers are integral members of the treatment teams. The Treatment Teams reflects a culture of cooperation, enthusiasm, and mutual respect. The Social Worker’s primary role is to provide inpatient psychiatric patient care and supportive services that are directed at achieving successful patient outcomes and maximizing patient involvement in their own care plans. Patients and their families will experience the benefits of patient-focused psychiatric inpatient care through the integrated skills of all treatment team members. POSITION SUMMARY OSUWMC Hospital Harding inpatient psychiatric social workers practice with adult or adolescent patients admitted to the Harding Hospital psychiatric inpatient units who have been hospitalized for debilitating or dangerous psychological and/or behavioral issues, such as severe depression, mania, psychosis, suicidal, homicidal, catatonia, co-morbid substance use, and other conditions. Inpatient psychiatric social workers are an integral part of the multi-disciplinary team of psychiatrists, nurses, PCRMs, other social workers, medical, nursing, and social-work students & psychiatry residents, making recommendations for treatment, rehabilitation, and social service connections. Each patient admitted to OSU Harding is assigned a Psychiatric Inpatient Social Worker to manage their psychosocial needs during the admission. Each Inpatient Psychiatric Social worker maintains a caseload of patients to manage in collaboration with the attending psychiatrists and other members of the treatment team. The Inpatient Psychiatric Social Worker provides services to patients and/or families who receive inpatient psychiatric treatment. Psychiatric Inpatient Social Work duties include completing comprehensive mental health & drug and alcohol diagnostic assessments utilizing the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM-5) and ICD-10. Conducting ongoing evidenced-based suicide, crisis, and risk assessments. developing personalized, evidenced based treatment plans, conducting evidenced based interventions and groups to patients and families, providing crisis intervention and patient/family education. Social Workers work within the Interdisciplinary Treatment Team to provide these functions, and also provide discharge planning to facilitate the transition from hospital treatment to continuing care in the community following inpatient treatment. If appropriate, Inpatient Psychiatric Social Workers provide other case management services, including linkage and access to necessary support services (e.g. transportation, financial benefits, medical and legal services, and community resources such as emergency food, clothing, shelter, etc.) The Inpatient Psychiatric Social Worker is responsible for serving populations with a variety of clinical, religious and cultural needs. Inpatient Psychiatric Social Worker collaboratively work with patients and team members in an effort maximize patient’s potential for the healthiest coping responses to their challenging situations, including timely and safe discharge plans. Minimum Qualifications For Hire: Master’s degree in Social Work or Professional Counseling or related field and valid Ohio licensure (LSW or LPC) required. Eligibility for future independent licensure required. Independent licensure (LISW or LPCC) preferred. Pre or Post-Master’s training and experience in working with patients with mental illness and/or substance disorders is also required. Experience via an internship prior to completing Master’s level education may be considered. Experience with completing mental health & crisis assessments, case-management, and conducting evidenced based psychosocial interventions preferred. Must be willing to work weekends and holidays Function: Social and Behavioral Health Sub-Function: Social Work Band: Internal Resource Pool Level: C2 Additional Information: Location: Harding Hospital (0165) Position Type: Intermittent Scheduled Hours: 0.2 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Outpatient-CareAmbulatory/Nurse-Practitioner_R144584-1": {
      "title": "Nurse Practitioner",
