    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Supervisor---Specialized_R145109-1": {
      "title": "Supervisor - Specialized",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Supervisor - Specialized Department: Business Advancement | Schottenstein Center Guest Services Administration-JM Responsibilities Provide excellent guest service to fans attending Ohio State events Responsible for specialized area of event operations (backstage security, barricade/stage security, field/court security, Welcome Center, Ohio Stadium Tours) Provide direct supervision and oversight of event staff within specialized area of operation Act as a liaison with outside entities (tour security/management, visiting teams and coaches, officials, Learfield, etc.) Supervise multiple sport seasons (such as baseball, wrestling, lacrosse, etc.) Schedule event staff during an assigned athletic or special event, based on deployments provided by Event Management staff Verify attendance of staff and complete timesheets for events Attend annual Operations Meetings for assigned sports Participate in emergency drills or table top exercises produced by the Department of Public Safety Provide direct supervision to assigned crew of event staff at each event Ensure excellent guest service is being provided to guests by your staff Act as a second level of support to event staff to resolve guest issues in your assigned area Provide direct coaching and training to the staff assigned to your area Ensure that the staff assigned to you comply with policies & procedures included in the Event Staff Pocket Guide/Manual Scanning, counting and checking tickets at athletic contests and special events Conducting security screening of guests entering our facilities Provide excellent guest service to fans attending Ohio State events Directing and assisting guests to their seats or to find other amenities provided inside the facility Directing and assisting guests to services outside of the facility (roadways, restaurants, hotels, etc.) Assist with the enforcement of NCAA, Conference, University, and Athletic Department rules and regulations Recognize and check credentials, limit access to restricted areas of facilities Be an expert of and an advocate for Ohio State Athletics & the Schottenstein Center Qualifications Must be 18 years of age or older Minimum 5 years of experience as an event staff member, or equivalent Minimum 3 years working in specialized area of responsibility (backstage security, barricade/stage security, field/court security, Welcome Center, Ohio Stadium Tours) Experience managing others Must be able to stand on your feet for 4 hours or more, indoors and outdoors, rain or shine Ability to maintain a positive attitude at events at all times Ability to focus on listening and satisfying our guests Ability to maintain and support open communication with Event Management staff An interest in working with guests and fellow staff of varying backgrounds Excellent verbal communication skills Excellent problem solving ability Additional Information: Location: Schottenstein Center (0081) Position Type: Intermittent Scheduled Hours: 0.2 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Dean-s-Distinguished-Postdoctoral-Fellowship-in-Chemical-Biology-and-Drug-Discovery_R154685-1": {
      "title": "Dean’s Distinguished Postdoctoral Fellowship in Chemical Biology and Drug Discovery",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Dean’s Distinguished Postdoctoral Fellowship in Chemical Biology and Drug Discovery Department: Pharmacy | Medicinal Chemistry Buckeye BioLaunch, a newly established AI-enabled Center for Therapeutic Discovery and Development in the College of Pharmacy at The Ohio State University, invites applications for the Dean’s Distinguished Postdoctoral Fellowship in the broad area of Chemical Biology and Drug Discovery. We seek outstanding early-career scientists whose research advances fundamental understanding of biological systems while creating new opportunities for therapeutic discovery and development. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in biochemical, biophysical, cellular, structural, and/or proteomic approaches to study target engagement, target validation, molecular recognition, drug action, and protein–ligand interactions. Additional Information: Minimum Qualifications: •             Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree in chemistry, chemical biology, biochemistry, biophysics, pharmacology, molecular biology, structural biology, bioengineering, or a closely related field. •             Applicants must have completed all requirements for the doctoral degree before beginning the fellowship. Candidates should be no more than five years beyond receipt of their highest terminal degree at the time of application. Desired Qualifications: Expertise in one or more areas relevant to chemical biology, drug discovery, target engagement, target validation, protein–ligand interactions, structural biology, proteomics, or translational therapeutic discovery. Location: Parks Hall (0273) Position Type: Term (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 40 Shift: First Shift Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Golf-Outside-Operations_R146050": {
      "title": "Golf Outside Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Golf Outside Operations Department: Athletics | Golf Course Pro Shop-JM The Outside Operations staff’s main job is knowledge, hospitality, and customer service . The outside operations staff is the first and last point of contact of members and guests of The Ohio State University Golf Club. It is of the upmost importance for the staff to make sure that they are always attentive to members and guests needs.  The responsibility of the outside operations staff is to greet all patrons first, in a friendly and professional manner. The outside operations staff is also in charge of the cleaning and refilling of all restroom supplies in the clubhouse.  You will be required to vacuum the entire clubhouse area, take out the trash, and report any issues you encounter to the professional staff.  You also may be required to do basic maintenance tasks such as changing light bulbs and unclogging toilets.  Another area you will be responsible for cleaning is the team building.  Outside Operations staff members will be required to be knowledgeable of all duties they are required to complete and if they have any questions they can ask a member of the professional staff.  Outside Operations staff members are also required for picking up/cleaning balls and basic maintenance of the range.    Additional Information: Location: OSU Golf Club - Kepler Club House (0033) Position Type: Intermittent Scheduled Hours: 0.2 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
    },
    "https://osu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Columbus-Campus/Fall-Semester-Temporary-Sales-Assistant_R149938-1": {
      "title": "Fall Semester Temporary Sales Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nScreen reader users may encounter difficulty with this site. For assistance with applying, please contact hr-accessibleapplication@osu.edu . If you have questions while submitting an application, please review these frequently asked questions . Current Employees and Students: If you are currently employed or enrolled as a student at The Ohio State University, please l og in to Workday to use the internal application process. Welcome to The Ohio State University's career site.  We invite you to apply to positions of interest. In order to ensure your application is complete, you must complete the following: Ensure you have all necessary documents available when starting the application process. You can review the additional job description section on postings for documents that may be required. Prior to submitting your application, please review and update (if necessary) the information in your candidate profile as it will transfer to your application.  Job Title: Fall Semester Temporary Sales Assistant Department: Student Life | Dining Services Job Description The Sales Assistant supports the dining operation serving students, staff and guests of The Ohio State University; greets and serves customers; operates coffee equipment, makes gourmet coffee and specialty drinks; prepares and handles food and beverage orders; collects payment by cash, credit or Buck ID, prepares sales reports; takes daily inventory; stocks shelves, freezers, and coolers; maintains a clean and sanitary service and work area; position makes decisions based on established policies and procedures under the direction of the supervisor. This is a temporary staff position that is not to exceed 12 months. Qualifications Required: High school diploma or GED; ability to communicate effectively; successful completion of a background check. Desired: 0-2 years of front-line customer service experience; 1 year of experience taking and filling food orders; 1 year of experience brewing premium coffees and making espresso-based drinks; 1 year of cash handling experience; 1 year of experience in taking inventories; 1 year of experience in placing orders or requisitioning supplies. Additional Information: Additional Job Description The Ohio State University’s Student Life Dining Services is a premier campus dining department dedicated to serving students, staff, faculty and guests. Critical to the Residential Experience, Dining Services administers the student meal plan to approximately 15,000 residential students on the Columbus, Mansfield, Marion, Newark and Wooster campuses. Compensation The target hiring range for this position is $17.00. Student Life Mission The Office of Student Life fosters students’ development, learning, well-being and sense of belonging; empowers students to achieve their academic, personal and professional goals; and prepares students to be engaged in a global society. Location: Kennedy Commons (0105) Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Scheduled Hours: 25 Shift: Varying Shifts Final candidates are subject to successful completion of a background check.  A drug screen or physical may be required during the post offer process. Thank you for your interest in positions at The Ohio State University and Wexner Medical Center. Once you have applied, the most updated information on the status of your application can be found by visiting the Candidate Home section of this site. Please view your submitted applications by logging in and reviewing your status. For answers to additional questions please review the frequently asked questions . The university is an equal opportunity employer, including veterans and disability."
